 "MY-H3896": {
  "lawId": "MY-H3896",
  "sourceLang": "ms",
  "targetLang": "en",
  "engine": "official-extract",
  "model": null,
  "promptVersion": null,
  "translatedAt": "2026-10-28",
  "reviewed": "official",
  "note": "公报原生英文版（与马来文版同一公报并置），逐字照录，非机译。",
  "articles": [
   {
    "no": 1,
    "text": {
     "en": "1. (1) These regulations may be cited as the Food (Amendment)\n\nRegulations 2018.\n\n(2) These Regulations come into operation on 30 September 2020.\n\nAmendment of regulation 285"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 1"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 2,
    "text": {
     "en": "2. The Food Regulations 1985 [P.U. (A) 437/1985] are amended in regulation 285—\n\n(a) by substituting for subregulation (2) the following subregulation:\n\n\"(2) No person shall manufacture for sale, sell, expose or\n\noffer for sale, consign or deliver table salt or salt weighing 20 kg or\n\nless unless the table salt or salt is iodised table salt or salt referred\n\nto in subregulation (1A) and the table salt or salt shall be labelled\n\nwith the words \"Iodised Table Salt\" or \"Iodised Salt\" as the case\n\nmaybe, on each of its package.\"; and\n\n(b) by substituting for subregulation (3) the following subregulation:\n\n\"(3) The Minister may, by notification in the Gazette,\n\ndirect that in certain areas as designated by the Director or any\n\nauthorised officer, no person shall manufacture for sale, sell,\n\nexpose or offer for sale, consign or deliver table salt or salt\n\nweighing more than 20 kg for household use and human\n\nconsumption unless it is iodised table salt or iodised salt.\".\n\nMade 7 September 2018\n\n[KKM. 600-1/1/35; PN(PU2)418/XXIV]\n\nDATUK SERI DR. DZULKEFLY BIN AHMAD\n\nMinister of Health"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 2"
    }
   }
  ]
 },
 "MY-H3897": {
  "lawId": "MY-H3897",
  "sourceLang": "ms",
  "targetLang": "en",
  "engine": "official-extract",
  "model": null,
  "promptVersion": null,
  "translatedAt": "2026-10-28",
  "reviewed": "official",
  "note": "公报原生英文版（与马来文版同一公报并置），逐字照录，非机译。",
  "articles": [
   {
    "no": 1,
    "text": {
     "en": "1. This order may be cited as the Co-operative Societies (Assumption of Control)\n(Appointment) (No. 2) Order 2019.\n\nAssumption of control"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 1"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 2,
    "text": {
     "en": "2. The Commission appoints Kastian bin Dhula to assume control of the whole of the\nproperty, business, activities and affairs of the Koperasi Pekerja-Pekerja Kerajaan Sabah\nBerhad and carry on the whole of its business, activities and affairs with effect\nfrom 30 October 2019 to 29 October 2021 or until a Board is elected under the  by-laws\nof the co-operative society, whichever is earlier.\n\nCosts and expenses"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 2"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 3,
    "text": {
     "en": "3. Any costs and expenses incurred by the Commission in relation to the assumption\nof control under paragraph 2 shall be payable out of the funds and properties of the\nKoperasi Pekerja-Pekerja Kerajaan Sabah Berhad as a first charge.\n\nMade 29 October 2019\n[SKM.IP(SULIT)KP: 1665/1/5; PN(PU2)527/XIX]\n\nDATUK NORDIN BIN SALLEH\nExecutive Chairman\nMalaysia Co-operative Societies Commission"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 3"
    }
   }
  ]
 },
 "MY-H3899": {
  "lawId": "MY-H3899",
  "sourceLang": "ms",
  "targetLang": "en",
  "engine": "official-extract",
  "model": null,
  "promptVersion": null,
  "translatedAt": "2026-10-28",
  "reviewed": "official",
  "note": "公报原生英文版（与马来文版同一公报并置），逐字照录，非机译。",
  "articles": [
   {
    "no": 1,
    "text": {
     "en": "1. (1)  These rules may be cited as the Income Tax (Accelerated Capital\nAllowance) (Excursion Bus) Rules 2021.\n\n(2) These Rules has effect from the year of assessment 2020 until\nthe year of assessment 2021.\n\nApplication"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 1"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 2,
    "text": {
     "en": "2. (1)    These Rules shall apply to a licensed tour operator—\n\n(a) resident in Malaysia;\n\n(b) who has incurred capital expenditure for the purchase\nof an excursion bus as the first registered owner in the basis period\nfor a year of assessment from a source consisting of his business\nin relation to the tour operations; and\n\n(c) who is a holder of the tourism vehicle licence issued\nunder the Land Public Transport Act 2010 [ Act 715 ] or\nthe Tourism Vehicles Licensing Act 1999 [Act 594].\n\n(2) The excursion bus purchased by the licensed tour operator shall—\n\n(a) be used exclusively for the conveyance of tourists pursuant to\nthe Land Public Transport Act 2010 or the Tourism Vehicles\nLicensing Act 1999;\n\n(b) be assembled or constructed in Malaysia pursuant to Motor Vehicles\n(Registration and Licensing) Rules 1959 [L. N. 173/1959]; and\n\n(c)  is not a recondition excursion bus.\n\nInterpretation"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 2"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 3,
    "text": {
     "en": "3. In these Rules, \"licensed tour operator\" has the same meaning assigned\nto it under section 2 of the Tourism Industry Act 1992 [Act 482].\n\nDeeming provision relating to hire purchase agreement"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 3"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 4,
    "text": {
     "en": "4. For the purposes of these Rules, w here the licensed tour operator incurs\ncapital expenditure under a hire purchase agreement for the purchase of\nan excursion bus for the purpose of tour operations—\n\n(a) the licensed tour operator shall be treated as the owner of that\nexcursion bus; and\n\n(b) the capital expenditure incurred by the licensed tour operator in the\nbasis period for the year of assessment shall be taken to be capital portion\nof any instalment payment or, where there is more than one such payment,\nof the aggregate of those payments made by the licensed tour operator\nunder such hire purchase agreement in that basis period.\n\nInitial allowance"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 4"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 5,
    "text": {
     "en": "5. The licensed tour operator qualifies for an initial allowanc e provided und er\nparagraph 10 of Schedule 3 to  the Act which shall be equal to one -fifth of the\ncapital expenditure incurred for the purchase of the excursion bus.\n\nAnnual allowance"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 5"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 6,
    "text": {
     "en": "6. The licensed tour operator qualifies for an annual allowance provided u nder\nparagraph 15 of Schedule 3 to  the Act which shall be equal to two -fifths of the\ncapital expenditure incurred for the purchase of the excursion bus.\n\nNon-application"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 6"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 7,
    "text": {
     "en": "7. These Rules shall not apply to a licensed tour operator who has incurred\ncapital expenditure for the purchase of the excursion bus in a basis period for the\nyear of assessment where during that basis period the licensed tour operator is eligible\nand has claimed in respect of the purchase of the excursion bus—\n\n(a) investment tax a llowance under the Promotion of Investments Act 1986\n[Act 327];\n\n(b) reinvestment allowance under Schedule 7A to the Act;\n\n(c) investment allowance for service sector under Schedule 7B to the Act;\n\n(d) accelerated capital allowance under any rules made under section 1 54\nof the Act; or\n\n(e) tax exemption under any order made under paragraph  127(3)(b)\nor subsection 127(3 A) of the Act  in respect of his statutory income\nwhich is equivalent to any part or the whole of the amount of the qualifying\ncapital expenditure incurred by the licensed tour operator.\n\nMade 29 June 2021\n[MOF.TAX(S)7-1/3/54; LHDN.AY.A.600-12/1/7(29)-40; PN(PU2)80/Jld. 101]\n\n   TENGKU DATUK SERI UTAMA ZAFRUL BIN TENGKU ABDUL AZIZ\n                                              Minister of Finance\n\n[To be laid before the Dewan Rakyat pursuant to subsection 154(2) of the\nIncome Tax Act 1967]"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 7"
    }
   }
  ]
 },
