 "MY-H3913": {
  "lawId": "MY-H3913",
  "sourceLang": "ms",
  "targetLang": "en",
  "engine": "official-extract",
  "model": null,
  "promptVersion": null,
  "translatedAt": "2026-10-28",
  "reviewed": "official",
  "note": "公报原生英文版（与马来文版同一公报并置），逐字照录，非机译。",
  "articles": [
   {
    "no": 1,
    "text": {
     "en": "1. These regulations may be cited as the Prevention and Control of Infectious\n\nDiseases (Measures within Infected Local Areas) (No. 8) (Amendment)\n\nRegulations 2020.\n\nNew regulation 4A"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 1"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 2,
    "text": {
     "en": "2. The Prevention and Control of Infectious Diseases (Measures within Infected\n\nLocal Areas) (No. 8) Regulations 2020 [P.U. (A) 254/2020] are amended by inserting after\n\nregulation 4 the following regulation:\n\n\"Control of movement within the State of Sabah"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 2"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 4,
    "text": {
     "en": "4A. There shall be control of movement within the State of Sabah for the period\n\nfrom 3 October 2020 to 16 October 2020 as follows:\n\n(a) a person may move within any district, from one place to\n\nanother place; and\n\n(b) no person shall move from one district to another district except\n\nwith prior written permission of the police officer in charge of\n\nthe police station nearest to the residence of such person.\".\n\nMade 1 October 2020\n\n[KKM.600-29/4/146 Jld.2 (30); PN(PU2)470/IV]\n\n DATO' SRI DR. ADHAM BIN BABA\n\nMinister of Health"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 4"
    }
   }
  ]
 },
 "MY-H3916": {
  "lawId": "MY-H3916",
  "sourceLang": "ms",
  "targetLang": "en",
  "engine": "official-extract",
  "model": null,
  "promptVersion": null,
  "translatedAt": "2026-10-28",
  "reviewed": "official",
  "note": "公报原生英文版（与马来文版同一公报并置），逐字照录，非机译。",
  "articles": [
   {
    "no": 1,
    "text": {
     "en": "1. This order may be cited as the Occupational Safety and Health\n\n(Exemption for Plant Requiring Certificate of Fitness at the Place of Work of\n\nPETRONAS within Maritime Zones) Order 2024.\n\nInterpretation"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 1"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 2,
    "text": {
     "en": "2. In this Order—\n\n\"plant requiring certificate of fitness\" has the meaning assigned to it\n\nin the Occupational Safety and Health (Plant Requiring Certificate of Fitness)\n\nRegulations 2024 [P.U. (A) 99/2024];\n\n\"PETRONAS\" means Petroliam Nasional Berhad as referred to in subsection 3(1)\n\nof the Petroleum Development Act 1974 [Act 144];\n\n\"recognized standard\" has the meaning assigned to it in the Occupational Safety\n\nand Health (Plant Requiring Certificate of Fitness) Regulations 2024;\n\n\"maritime zones\" has the meaning assigned to it in the Baselines of Maritime\n\nZones Act 2006 [Act 660].\n\nExemption"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 2"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 3,
    "text": {
     "en": "3. The Minister exempts every plant requiring certificate of fitness at the place of\n\nwork owned by PETRONAS within the maritime zones from the application of\n\nsections 27C, 27D and 27E of the Act and the Occupational Safety and Health\n\n(Plant Requiring Certificate of Fitness) Regulations 2024.\n\nConditions of exemption"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 3"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 4,
    "text": {
     "en": "4. The exemption under paragraph 3 is subject to the conditions\n\nthat PETRONAS shall—\n\n(a) establish a regulatory body for the purposes of management of every plant\n\nrequiring certificate of fitness at the place of work owned\n\nby PETRONAS within the maritime zones;\n\n(b) submit its annual work plan in respect of the management of the integrity\n\nof the plant requiring certificate of fitness to the Director General;\n\n(c) ensure that the plant requiring certificate of fitness is designed,\n\nconstructed, installed, tested and inspected in accordance with\n\nrecognized standard;\n\n(d) ensure that only qualified individuals are in charge of or involved\n\nin the installation, erection, dismantling, testing, inspection, maintenance,\n\nrepair, servicing, operation or handling of, or attendance on, the plant\n\nrequiring certificate of fitness;\n\n(e) ensure that the plant requiring certificate of fitness is inspected\n\nby an inspector who has been verified by the Director General; and\n\n(f) ensure that any record relating to the plant requiring certificate of fitness\n\nis properly maintained and shall be submitted for inspection\n\nupon direction by the Director General.\n\nMade 4 October 2024\n\n[KSM.PUU(S)600-1/2/9/8(10); PN(PU2)541/JLD.14]\n\nSIM CHEE KEONG\n\nMinister of Human Resources"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 4"
    }
   }
  ]
 },
