 "MY-H3985": {
  "lawId": "MY-H3985",
  "sourceLang": "ms",
  "targetLang": "en",
  "engine": "official-extract",
  "model": null,
  "promptVersion": null,
  "translatedAt": "2026-10-28",
  "reviewed": "official",
  "note": "公报原生英文版（与马来文版同一公报并置），逐字照录，非机译。",
  "articles": [
   {
    "no": 1,
    "text": {
     "en": "1. (1) These regulations may be cited as the Prevention and Control of\n\nInfectious Diseases (Measures within Infected Local Areas) (No. 8) (Amendment)\n\n(No. 2) Regulations 2020.\n\n(2) These Regulations come into operation on 7 October 2020.\n\nNew regulation 3A"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 1"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 2,
    "text": {
     "en": "2. The Prevention and Control of Infectious Diseases (Measures within Infected\n\nLocal Areas) (No. 8) Regulations 2020 [P.U. (A) 254/2020], which are referred to as the\n\n\"principal Regulations\" in these Regulations, are amended by inserting after regulation 3\n\nthe following regulation:\n\n\"Prohibition on movement to place that is subject to conditional movement\n\ncontrol order"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 2"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 3,
    "text": {
     "en": "3A. (1) No person shall enter into or exit from a place that is subject to\n\na conditional movement control order except any person who is given permission\n\nby an authorized officer.\n\n(2) For the purposes of subregulation (1), \"conditional movement\n\ncontrol order\" refers to a direction given by an authorized officer under\n\nsubsection 11(3) of the Act.\".\n\nNew regulation 4B\n\n3. The principal Regulations are amended by inserting after regulation 4A the\n\nfollowing regulation:\n\n\"Control of movement from the State of Sabah"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 3"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 4,
    "text": {
     "en": "4B. (1) For the period from 12 October 2020 to 25 October 2020, no person\n\nshall move from the State of Sabah to the State of Sarawak, the Federal Territory\n\nof Labuan or any state in Peninsular Malaysia.\n\n(2) Where, due to a special and particular reason, a person needs to\n\nmove from the State of Sabah to the State of Sarawak, the Federal Territory of\n\nLabuan or any state in Peninsular Malaysia, that person shall obtain prior written\n\npermission of the police officer in charge of the police station nearest to the\n\nresidence of such person.\".\n\nMade 7 October 2020\n\n[KKM.600-29/4/146 Jld.2 (30); PN(PU2)470/IV]\n\n DATO' SRI DR. ADHAM BIN BABA\n\nMinister of Health"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 4"
    }
   }
  ]
 },
