 "MY-H4059": {
  "lawId": "MY-H4059",
  "sourceLang": "ms",
  "targetLang": "en",
  "engine": "official-extract",
  "model": null,
  "promptVersion": null,
  "translatedAt": "2026-10-28",
  "reviewed": "official",
  "note": "公报原生英文版（与马来文版同一公报并置），逐字照录，非机译。",
  "articles": [
   {
    "no": 1,
    "text": {
     "en": "1. (1) These rules may be cited as the Employees Provident Fund\n\n(Amendment) (No. 3) Rules 2021.\n\n (2) These Rules come into operation on 1 October 2021.\n\nAmendment of rule 41"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 1"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 2,
    "text": {
     "en": "2. The Employees Provident Fund Rules 1991 [P.U. (A) 493/1991] are amended\n\nin rule 41 by inserting after subrule (10T) the following subrules:\n\n(10U) Where a notice of withdrawal is made under\n\nparagraph 54(6)(j) of the Act on the ground that a member of\n\nthe Fund takes an insurance policy or a takaful certificate\n\nfor himself, or himself and any approved person, the member of\n\nthe Fund shall give a notice of withdrawal to the Board\n\nin accordance with any manner as determined by the Board.\n\n(10V) The notice of withdrawal made under\n\nsubrule (10U) shall be accompanied with any document\n\nrelating to the insurance policy or takaful certificate as evidence\n\nin support of the notice of withdrawal.\n\n(10W) Where the Board is satisfied with the notice of\n\nwithdrawal made under subrule (10U), the Board may—\n\n(a) authorize the withdrawal from Account II of\n\nthe member of the Fund; and\n\n\"Member of\n\nFund takes\n\ninsurance\n\npolicy or\n\ntakaful\n\ncertificate.\n\n(b) pay partly or wholly the sum required for\n\nthe taking of insurance policy or\n\ntakaful certificate subject to the amount\n\nstanding to the credit in Account II of\n\nthe member of the Fund.\n\n(10X) The sum referred to in paragraph (10W)(b) shall be\n\npaid on a yearly basis to an insurance or a takaful company.\n\n(10Y) The Board may, at any time before the expiry of\n\nthe insurance policy or takaful certificate, cease to make\n\npayment for the sum referred to in paragraph (10W)(b)\n\nif the member of the Fund—\n\n(a) revokes the notice of withdrawal; or\n\n(b) cancels the insurance policy or\n\ntakaful certificate taken from the insurance or\n\ntakaful company.\n\n(10Z) Where the member of the Fund cancels the\n\ninsurance policy or takaful certificate taken from the insurance\n\nor takaful company, the insurance or takaful company shall,\n\nwithin the period as determined by the Board, refund\n\nthe unallocated sum for the purpose of taking the\n\ninsurance policy or takaful certificate to the Board.\n\n(10ZA) For the purposes of subrule (10U) and\n\nthis subrule—\n\n(a) \"approved person\" means child or spouse of\n\nthe member of the Fund;\n\n(b) \"child\" has the meaning assigned to it\n\nin subrule (10E) of these Rules; and\n\n(c) \"spouse\" has the meaning assigned to it\n\nin paragraph (10M)(d) of these Rules.\".\n\nMade 2 July 2021\n\n[KWSP/JUU/9/1/GUB(U)33; PN(PU2)498/Jld.17]\n\n TAN SRI AHMAD BADRI BIN MOHD ZAHIR\n\n Chairman\n\n Employees Provident Fund Board"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 2"
    }
   }
  ]
 },
