 "MY-H4223": {
  "lawId": "MY-H4223",
  "sourceLang": "ms",
  "targetLang": "en",
  "engine": "official-extract",
  "model": null,
  "promptVersion": null,
  "translatedAt": "2026-10-28",
  "reviewed": "official",
  "note": "公报原生英文版（与马来文版同一公报并置），逐字照录，非机译。",
  "articles": [
   {
    "no": 1,
    "text": {
     "en": "1. (1) This order may be cited as the Income Tax  (Exemption) (No.  4)\nOrder 2018.\n\n(2) This Order is deemed to have come into operation from the year of\nassessment 2018.\n\nApplication"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 1"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 2,
    "text": {
     "en": "2. This Order shall apply to a member institution specified in subsection 36(2) of the\nMalaysia Deposit Insurance Corporation Act 2011 [Act 720].\n\nExemption"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 2"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 3,
    "text": {
     "en": "3. (1) The Minister exempts a member institution in the basis period for a year of\nassessment from the payment of income tax in respect of the statutory income of a\nshareholders' fund that is derived from a business referred to in subparagraph (2) which\nis equiva lent to the f irst levy or annual levy paid from  the shareholders' fund to the\nMalaysia Deposit Insurance Corporation for that year of assessment.\n\n(2)    The business referred to in subparagraph (1) is a business in relation to—\n\n(a)     a life fund;\n\n(b) a family fund;\n\n(c) a general fund;\n\n(d) any composite insurance business which consist s of a life fund and\na general fund; or\n\n(e) any composite takaful business which consist s of a family fund\nand a general fund.\n\n (3) Where, by reason of the absence or insufficiency of the statutory income,\nexemption cannot be granted or cannot be granted in full as the member institution is\nentitled under subparagraph (1) for that year of assessment, then so much of the\nstatutory income in respect of which exemption cannot be granted for that year of\nassessment, shall be granted exemption for the first subsequent year of assessment for\nthe basis period for which the member institution ha s statutory income of the\nshareholders' fund that is derived from a business referred to in subparagraph (2) , and\nfor the subsequent year or years of assessment until the exemption is granted in respect\nof the whole statutory income as the member institution  is entitled under\nsubparagraph (1).\n\n (4) For the purpose of this paragraph—\n\n(a) \"first levy\" means any levy payable by the  member institution  to th e\nMalaysia Deposit Insurance Corporation pursuant to section 71 of the\nMalaysia Deposit Insurance Corporation Act 2011; and\n\n(b) \"annual levy\" means any levy payable  by the member institution to the\nMalaysia Deposit Insurance Corporation pursuant to sections 72 and 73\nof the Malaysia Deposit Insurance Corporation Act 2011.\n\nMade 23 November 2018\n[Perb. (8.09) 248/40/7-1411 VOL.2(51); LHDN.01/35/(S)/42/51/286-39; PN(PU2)80/XCI]\n\nLIM GUAN ENG\nMinister of Finance\n\n[To be laid before the Dewan Rakyat pursuant to subsection 127(4) of the Income Tax\nAct 1967]"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 3"
    }
   }
  ]
 },
