 "MY-H4321": {
  "lawId": "MY-H4321",
  "sourceLang": "ms",
  "targetLang": "en",
  "engine": "official-extract",
  "model": null,
  "promptVersion": null,
  "translatedAt": "2026-10-28",
  "reviewed": "official",
  "note": "公报原生英文版（与马来文版同一公报并置），逐字照录，非机译。",
  "articles": [
   {
    "no": 1,
    "text": {
     "en": "1. (1) These regulations may be cited as the Petroleum (Income Tax)\n(PETRONAS Marginal Field) Regulations 2014.\n\n(2)   These Regulations are deemed to  have come into operation on\n30   November 2010.\n\nInterpretation"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 1"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 2,
    "text": {
     "en": "2. (1) In these Regulations , \"PETRONAS marginal field\" means a field as\ndetermined under regulation 3.\n\n(2) For the purposes of these Regulations, \"PETRONAS\" is an abbreviation for\nthe Petroliam Nasiona l Berhad as referred to in subsection 3(1) of the Petroleum\nDevelopment Act 1974 [Act 144].\n\nPETRONAS marginal field"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 2"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 3,
    "text": {
     "en": "3. The Minister may determine a PETRONAS marginal field which is a field\noperated solely by PETRONAS which has potential crude oil reserves  not exceeding\nthirty million stock tank barrels or natural gas reserves not exceeding five hundred\nbillion standard cubic feet.\n\nGross income"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 3"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 4,
    "text": {
     "en": "4. (1) In ascertaining the gross income of PETRONAS from its\npetroleum operations carried on in a PETRONAS marginal field, income from petroleum\noperations in a PETRONAS marginal field shall be treated separately from its other\npetroleum operations.\n\n(2)  Where PETRONAS carries on petroleum operations in two or more\nPETRONAS marginal fields, income from all those PET RONAS marginal fields shall be\ntaken as the total gross income of PETRONAS from all those fields.\n\nAdjusted income"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 4"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 5,
    "text": {
     "en": "5. The adjusted income of PETRONAS for the basis period for a year of assessment\nfrom its petroleum operations in a PETRONAS marginal field s hall be an amount\nascertained in accordance with Chapter 3 of Part III of the Act.\n\nAdjusted loss"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 5"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 6,
    "text": {
     "en": "6. (1)  Where but for an insufficiency of gross income of PETRONAS for the basis\nperiod for a year of assessment from its petroleum operations in a PETRONAS m arginal\nfield there would have been an amount of adjusted income of PETRONAS for that\nperiod, the amount by which the total of all such deductions as would then have been\nallowed under Chapter 3 of Part III of the Act in ascertaining that adjusted income\nexceeds its gross income for that period from its petroleum operations in that\nPETRONAS marginal field shall be taken to be the amount of its adjusted loss for that\nperiod from that petroleum operations.\n\n(2)  The adjusted loss ascertained under subregulati on (1) shall only be\nallowed as a deduction against the statutory income of PETRONAS from its petroleum\noperations in a PETRONAS marginal field.\n\nStatutory income"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 6"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 7,
    "text": {
     "en": "7. Subject to regulations 8 and 9, the statutory income of PETRONAS for the basis\nperiod for a year of assessment in respect of petroleum operations in a PETRONAS\nmarginal field shall be ascertained in accordance with Chapter 4 of Part III of the Act\nand by having regard to the Petroleum (Income Tax) (Accelerated Capital Allowance)\n(PETRONAS Marginal Field) Rules 2014 [P.U. (A) 304/2014].\n\nUnabsorbed capital allowance"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 7"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 8,
    "text": {
     "en": "8. Where, by reason of the absence or insufficiency of the adjusted income of\nPETRONAS from its petroleum operations in a PETRONAS marginal field for the basis\nperiod for a year of  assessment, effect cannot be given or cannot be given in full to the\ncapital allowance to which PETRONAS is entitled under the Act  for that year of\nassessment, then so much of that allowance which cannot be made shall  be made in the\nfirst subsequent year of assessment for the basis period for which there is adjusted\nincome from petroleum operations in a PETRONAS marginal field, and for subsequent\nyears of assessment until the whole of the allowance to which PETRONAS is so entitled\nis made.\n\nAssessable income"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 8"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 9,
    "text": {
     "en": "9. (1) The assessable income of PETRONAS from petroleum operations in a\nPETRONAS marginal field for a year of assessment, which is referred to in these\nRegulations as \"the relevant year of assessment\", shall consist of the amount of its\nstatutory income for the relevant year of assessment from that petroleum operations in\na PETRONAS marginal field reduced by the amount of any adjusted loss from that\npetroleum operations for the basis period for the year of assessment preceding the\nrelevant year of assess ment which has not been deducted from its statutory income\nfrom that petroleum operations for a year of assessment  prior to the relevant year of\nassessment.\n\n(2) A deduction of any adjusted loss under subregulation (1) shall be made as\nfar as possible from th e statutory income of PETRONAS from its petroleum operations\nin a PETRONAS marginal field for the first year of assessment after that for the basis\nperiod for which that loss is the adjusted loss, and, so far as it cannot be so made, then\nthe deduction shall be made from the statutory income from that petroleum operations\nfor the subsequent year of assessment.\n\n(3) The assessable income ascertained under subregulation (1) shall be\ntreated as part of the chargeable income of PETRONAS for a year of assessment for  the\npurpose of section 22 of the Act.\n\nChargeable income"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 9"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 10,
    "text": {
     "en": "10. Subject to section 22 of the Act, the chargeable income of PETRONAS from\npetroleum operations in a PETRONAS marginal field for a year of assessment shall\nconsist of the amount of its assessable  income for that year of assessment from that\npetroleum operations in a PETRONAS marginal field reduced by an amount equal to any\ngift of money or the cost of contribution or value of contribution made by PETRONAS in\na basis period for that year of assessment which shall be determined in accordance with\nthe following formula:\n\nA      x       C\nB\n\n                          where          A is the gross income of PETRONAS from a PETRONAS\nmarginal field;\n\nB is the total gross income of PETRONAS from\npetroleum operations; and\n\nC is the gift of money or the cost of contribution or\nvalue of contribution made by PETRONAS in the\nbasis period for that year of assessment.\n\nSeparate account"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 10"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 11,
    "text": {
     "en": "11. PETRONAS shall maintain separate accounts for its income derived from a\nPETRONAS marginal field and for its income derived from its other petroleum\noperations.\n\nMade 17 November 2014\n[Perb. CR(8.09)681/2 -61(Sj.19) Jld. 3(Sk.2); LHDN. 01/35/(S)/42/51 Klt. 17;\nPN(PU2)474/III]\n\nTAN SRI DR. MOHD SHUKOR BIN MAHFAR\nDirector General of Inland Revenue"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 11"
    }
   }
  ]
 },
