 "MY-H4470": {
  "lawId": "MY-H4470",
  "sourceLang": "ms",
  "targetLang": "en",
  "engine": "official-extract",
  "model": null,
  "promptVersion": null,
  "translatedAt": "2026-10-28",
  "reviewed": "official",
  "note": "公报原生英文版（与马来文版同一公报并置），逐字照录，非机译。",
  "articles": [
   {
    "no": 1,
    "text": {
     "en": "1. (1) This order may be cited as the Price Control and Anti -Profiteering\n(Price Marking of Price-Controlled Goods) (No. 5) Order 2023.\n\n (2) This Order comes into operation on 1 November 2023.\n\nPrice marking"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 1"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 2,
    "text": {
     "en": "2. (1) Any person who sells or offers to sell any price -controlled goods\npublished in the Price Control and Anti-Profiteering (Determination of Maximum Price)\n(No. 14) Order 20 23 [P.U. (A) 325/2023] shall affix a pink coloured label indicating\nthe price per unit or per unit weight, the name describing such price-controlled goods\nand the grade or quality, if any, of such price-controlled goods.\n\n (2) Any person who fails to comply with subparagraph (1) commits\nan offence and shall, on conviction, be liable—\n\n(a) if such person is a body corporate, to a fine not exceeding\ntwenty thousand ringgit and, for a second or subsequent offence,\nto a fine not exceeding fifty thousand ringgit; or\n\n(b) if such person is not a body corporate, to a fine not exceeding\nten t housand ringgit and, for a second or subsequent offence,\nto a fine not exceeding twenty thousand ringgit.\n\nRevocation"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 2"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 3,
    "text": {
     "en": "3.  The Price Control and Anti -Profiteering (Price Marking of Price -Controlled\nGoods) (No. 8) Order 2022 [P.U. (A) 327/2022] is revoked.\n\nMade 27 October 2023\n[KPDN(PGK)(S)26/0.5001/1 Jld.12; PN(PU2)695/Jld. 33]\n\nDATUK ARMIZAN BIN MOHD ALI\nMinister of Domestic Trade and Cost of Living"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 3"
    }
   }
  ]
 },
 "MY-H4471": {
  "lawId": "MY-H4471",
  "sourceLang": "ms",
  "targetLang": "en",
  "engine": "official-extract",
  "model": null,
  "promptVersion": null,
  "translatedAt": "2026-10-28",
  "reviewed": "official",
  "note": "公报原生英文版（与马来文版同一公报并置），逐字照录，非机译。",
  "articles": [
   {
    "no": 1,
    "text": {
     "en": "1. These regulations may be cited as the Labuan Business Activity Tax\n\n(Requirements for Labuan International Commodity Trading Company)\n\n(Amendment) Regulations 2025.\n\nAmendment of regulation 3"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 1"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 2,
    "text": {
     "en": "2. The Labuan Business Activity Tax (Requirements for Labuan International\n\nCommodity Trading Company) Regulations 2021 [P.U. (A) 482/2021] are amended in\n\nregulation 3—\n\n(a) in paragraph (1)(a), by substituting for the words \"full-time employees\"\n\nthe words \"fit and proper full time employees\";\n\n(b) in paragraph (2)(a), by substituting for the words \"full-time employees\"\n\nwherever appearing the words \"fit and proper full time employees\";\n\n(c) in subregulation (3), by substituting for the words \"full-time employee\"\n\nthe words \"fit and proper full time employee\"; and\n\n(d) by inserting after subregulation (3) the following subregulation:\n\n\"(3A) For the purposes of paragraphs (1)(a) and (2)(a),\n\nand subregulation (3), the Labuan International Commodity Trading\n\nCompany shall comply with the conditions in relation to a fit and proper\n\nperson for full time employees as follows:\n\n(a) the employee shall carry out work that is\n\nappropriate in respect of the Labuan business\n\nactivities carried out by the Labuan International\n\nCommodity Trading Company;\n\n(b) the employee shall have adequate and\n\nappropriate competency and ability in respect of\n\nthe Labuan business activity carried out by the\n\nLabuan International Commodity Trading\n\nCompany;\n\n(c) the employee does not have any personal\n\ninterests or other responsibilities that may\n\ninterfere with the performance of his duties in\n\nrespect of the Labuan business activity carried out\n\nby the Labuan International Commodity Trading\n\nCompany;\n\n(d) the employee shall be employed on a permanent\n\nor contractual basis by the Labuan International\n\nCommodity Trading Company; and\n\n(e) the employee shall carry out his work with the\n\nLabuan International Commodity Trading\n\nCompany physically in Labuan.\".\n\nMade 2 September 2025\n\n[MOF.TAX(S)700-2/7/1289Jld.3; LHDN.AY.A 600-12/1/7(29)-408; PN(PU2)491/JLD.5]\n\nDATUK SERI AMIR HAMZAH BIN AZIZAN\n\nFinance Minister II"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 2"
    }
   }
  ]
 },
