 "MY-H4656": {
  "lawId": "MY-H4656",
  "sourceLang": "ms",
  "targetLang": "en",
  "engine": "official-extract",
  "model": null,
  "promptVersion": null,
  "translatedAt": "2026-10-28",
  "reviewed": "official",
  "note": "公报原生英文版（与马来文版同一公报并置），逐字照录，非机译。",
  "articles": [
   {
    "no": 1,
    "text": {
     "en": "1. This order may be cited as the Solicitors' Remuneration (Amendment)\n\nOrder 2016.\n\nGeneral amendment"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 1"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 2,
    "text": {
     "en": "2. The Solicitors' Remuneration Order 2005 [P.U. (A) 520/2005], which is referred\n\nto as the \"principal Order\" in this Order, is amended in the national language text by\n\nsubstituting for the word \"berhujah\" wherever appearing the word \"bertikaian\".\n\nAmendment of paragraph 3"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 2"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 3,
    "text": {
     "en": "3. Paragraph 3 of the principal Order is amended in subparagraph (k)\n\nby substituting for the word \"RM50\" the word \"RM100\".\n\nAmendment of First Schedule"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 3"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 4,
    "text": {
     "en": "4. The First Schedule to the principal Order is amended in rule 6 by substituting for\n\nthe words \"equivalent to the full scale fees specified in the Schedule\" the words\n\n\"of not more than 3% of the consideration sum\".\n\nAmendment of Third Schedule"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 4"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 5,
    "text": {
     "en": "5. The Third Schedule of the principal Order is amended—\n\n(a) by deleting the words \"the consideration as well as\" in subparagraphs (a),\n\n(b), (c) and (d); and\n\n(b) by inserting after rule 3 a proviso as follows:\n\n\"Provided that in relation to any Syariah compliant home purchase\n\nfinancing product not exceeding RM500,000.00, for which only the\n\nprincipal instrument or document is charged with ad valorem stamp duty,\n\nthen solely for purposes of this Schedule, any other instrument (other\n\nthan security documents) prepared in relation to the said home purchase\n\nfinancing product and required only for the purpose of compliance with\n\nSyariah principles shall be regarded as part of the principal instrument or\n\ndocument\".\n\nAmendment of Fifth Schedule"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 5"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 6,
    "text": {
     "en": "6. The Fifth Schedule to the princial Order is amended—\n\n(a) by substituting for subparagraph (d) the following subparagraph:\n\n\"(d) Real Property Gains Tax (CKHT)/CKHT\n\nforms (per form) (optional work done\n\nby a solicitor at the solicitor's\n\ndiscretion)\n\nNot less than:\n\n(i) Form 1A RM400\n\n(ii) Form 1A (each additional party) RM200\n\n(iii) Form 2A RM300\n\n(iv) Form 2A (each additional party) RM200\n\n(v) Form 3 RM100\n\n(vi) Form 3 (each additional party) RM100\n\n(vii)Form 502 – for each vendor RM150\n\nbut subject to the\n\nprovisions of rule 1 of\n\nthe Sixth Schedule\"\n\n(b) by substituting for subparagraph (e) the following subparagraph:\n\n\"(e) Income tax/LHDN (optional work done\n\nby a solicitor at the solicitor's\n\ndiscretion)\n\n Form CP 600 RM200\"\n\n(c) in subparagraph (h)—\n\n(i) by inserting before the word \"caveat\" the word \"private\"; and\n\n(ii) by inserting after the words \"loan transaction\" the words\n\n\"including the required statutory declaration\"; and\n\n(d) by inserting after subparagraph (i) the following subparagraphs:\n\n\"(j) Entry of trust caveat including the\n\nrequired statutory declaration\n\nRM500 for the first title\n\nand RM100 for each\n\nsubsequent title\n\n(k) Entry of lien holder's caveat RM400 for the first title\n\nand RM100 for each\n\nsubsequent title\n\n(l) Statutory declaration, e.g. not a\n\nbankrupt, own ocupation, error in\n\nname and the like\n\nRM100 per document\n\n(m) Transmission of deceased's property,\n\nvesting order and change of name at\n\nthe land office\n\nRM300 per application\n\nand RM100 for each\n\nsubsequent title\n\n(n) To certify a document Not exceeding RM25 for\n\nfirst certification and not\n\nexceeding RM10 each\n\nsubsequent certification\n\nof the same document\n\n(o) Application to the Economic Planning\n\nUnit of the Prime Minister's\n\nDepartment or similar regulatory\n\nbodies\n\nNot less than RM750 per\n\napplication but subject to\n\nthe provisions of rule 1 of\n\nthe Sixth Schedule\n\n(p) Issuing new letters of undertaking by\n\npurchaser's solicitors to financier's\n\nsolicitors\n\nRM100 per letter\"\n\nMade 28 September 2016\n\n[BC/M/16/2016 (BC/PA/C/112/2016); PN(PU2)314/XIV]\n\nYAA Tan Sri Dato' Seri Zulkefli bin Ahmad Makinudin Dato' A. Ramanathan\n\n Chief Judge of Malaya Advocate and Solicitor\n\n Dato' Amarjeet Singh A/L Serjit Singh Andrew Wong Fook Hin\n\n for the Attorney General of Malaysia Advocate and Solicitor\n\n Aslam bin Zainuddin Woon Yeow Thong\n\n for the Chief Registrar Advocate and Solicitor\n\n Hj. Abdul Murad bin Che Chik\n\n Advocate and Solicitor"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 6"
    }
   }
  ]
 },
 "MY-H4657": {
  "lawId": "MY-H4657",
  "sourceLang": "ms",
  "targetLang": "en",
  "engine": "official-extract",
  "model": null,
  "promptVersion": null,
  "translatedAt": "2026-10-28",
  "reviewed": "official",
  "note": "公报原生英文版（与马来文版同一公报并置），逐字照录，非机译。",
  "articles": [
   {
    "no": 1,
    "text": {
     "en": "1. (1) This order may be cited as the Medical Device (Declaration) Order 2017.\n\n(2) This Order comes into operation on 1 January 2018.\n\nInterpretation"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 1"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 2,
    "text": {
     "en": "2. In this Order, \"non-corrective contact lens\" means a contact lens which is not used\n\nto correct, remedy or relieve any refractive abnormalities or optical defects of sight.\n\nDeclaration"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 2"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 3,
    "text": {
     "en": "3. The Minister declares a non-corrective contact lens as a medical device.\n\nSavings and transitional"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 3"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 4,
    "text": {
     "en": "4. (1) An establishment who has imported, exported or placed in the market\n\na non-corrective contact lens before the date of coming into operation of this Order\n\nshall, within six months from the date of coming into operation of this Order, apply for\n\nthe registration of the non-corrective contact lens under section 6 of the Act and apply\n\nfor an establishment licence under section 16 of the Act.\n\n(2) An establishment who makes an application for registration of\n\nnon-corrective contact lens and for an establishment licence under subparagraph (1)\n\nmay continue to import, export or place in the market a non-corrective contact lens\n\npending determination of the application.\n\nMade 14 September 2017\n\n[KKM.PUU/PU2/MDA/3; PN(PU2)711/IV]\n\nDATUK SERI DR. S. SUBRAMANIAM\n\nMinister of Health"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 4"
    }
   }
  ]
 },
