 "MY-H4800": {
  "lawId": "MY-H4800",
  "sourceLang": "ms",
  "targetLang": "en",
  "engine": "official-extract",
  "model": null,
  "promptVersion": null,
  "translatedAt": "2026-10-28",
  "reviewed": "official",
  "note": "公报原生英文版（与马来文版同一公报并置），逐字照录，非机译。",
  "articles": [
   {
    "no": 1,
    "text": {
     "en": "1. (1) This order may be cited as the Immigration (Exemption) (No. 12)\n\nOrder 2026.\n\n(2) This Order comes into operation on 2 October 2026.\n\nDefinition"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 1"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 2,
    "text": {
     "en": "2. In this Order—\n\n\"designated area\" has the meaning assigned to it in the Johor Bahru–Singapore\n\nRapid Transit System Link Act 2026 [Act 884];\n\n\"Republic of Singapore enforcement officer\" has the meaning assigned to it\n\nin the Johor Bahru–Singapore Rapid Transit System Link Act 2026;\n\n\"Bukit Chagar Station\" has the meaning assigned to it in the\n\nJohor Bahru–Singapore Rapid Transit System Link Act 2026.\n\nExemption"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 2"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 3,
    "text": {
     "en": "3. The Minister exempts any Republic of Singapore enforcement officer from\n\nthe Immigration and Checkpoints Authority performing official duties in the\n\ndesignated area at Bukit Chagar Station from the application of a valid Pass\n\nissued under paragraph 6(1)(c) of the Act.\n\nConditions of exemption"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 3"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 4,
    "text": {
     "en": "4. Any Republic of Singapore enforcement officer who is exempted under\n\nparagraph 3 is subject to the following conditions:\n\n(a) the entry into Malaysia shall be to the designated area at Bukit Chagar\n\nStation;\n\n(b) possesses a valid travel document at all times;\n\n(c) for each entry into Malaysia to the designated area at Bukit Chagar Station,\n\nthe Republic of Singapore enforcement officer who is exempted shall,\n\nupon the request by the Government of Malaysia authorities, produce his\n\nsecurity pass or other evidence of identity for verification while performing\n\nofficial duties at Bukit Chagar Station; and\n\n(d) for each entry into Malaysia, the Republic of Singapore enforcement officer\n\nwho is exempted is only permitted to remain temporarily in Malaysia\n\nfor a period of not more than thirty days.\n\nMade 1 October 2026\n\n[KDN.IM.S.600-2/1/11 JLD.34(2); PN(PU2)100/JLD.20]\n\nDATUK SERI SAIFUDDIN NASUTION BIN ISMAIL\n\nMinister of Home Affairs"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 4"
    }
   }
  ]
 },
