 "MY-H4835": {
  "lawId": "MY-H4835",
  "sourceLang": "ms",
  "targetLang": "en",
  "engine": "official-extract",
  "model": null,
  "promptVersion": null,
  "translatedAt": "2026-10-28",
  "reviewed": "official",
  "note": "公报原生英文版（与马来文版同一公报并置），逐字照录，非机译。",
  "articles": [
   {
    "no": 1,
    "text": {
     "en": "1. (1) These rules may be cited as the Motor Vehicles (Prohibition of Certain\n\nTypes of Glass) (Amendment) Rules 2016.\n\n(2) These Rules come into operation on 6 February 2016.\n\nGeneral amendment"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 1"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 2,
    "text": {
     "en": "2. The Motor Vehicles (Prohibition of Certain Types of Glass) Rules 1991\n\n[P.U. (A) 39/1991], which are referred to as the \"principal Rules\" in these Rules, are\n\namended in the national language text, by substituting for the word \"benda\" wherever\n\nappearing the word \"bahan\".\n\nAmendment of rule 2"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 2"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 3,
    "text": {
     "en": "3. Rule 2 of the principal Rules is amended by inserting after the definition of\n\n\"authorised officer\" the following definiton:\n\n\" \" bus\" means a motor vehicle having a seating capacity of not less than eight\n\npersons including the driver;\".\n\nAmendment of rule 5"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 3"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 4,
    "text": {
     "en": "4. Rule 5 of the principal Rules is amended\n\n(a) by substituting for subrule (1) the following subrule:\n\n\"(1) A registered owner or driver of a motor vehicle of which the\n\nwindscreen of the motor vehicle is tinted, smeared, filmed over, sprayed,\n\npasted, fitted or otherwise treated or combined with any material or\n\nchemical shall ensure that the transmission through the windscreen of the\n\nmotor vehicle is at least seventy percent visible light.\";\n\n(b) by substituting for subrule (3) the following subrule:\n\n\"(3) A registered owner or driver of a motor vehicle of which the\n\nglass or other transparent material fitted to the front side, back side or\n\nrear of the motor vehicle is tinted, smeared, filmed over, sprayed, pasted,\n\nfitted or otherwise treated or combined with any material or chemical\n\nshall ensure that—\n\n(a) the transmission through the glass or other\n\ntransparent material fitted to the front side of the\n\nmotor vehicle is at least fifty percent visible light;\n\nand\n\n(b) the transmission through the glass or other\n\ntransparent material fitted to the back side and rear\n\nof the motor vehicle is at least thirty percent visible\n\nlight.\"; and\n\n(c) by substituting for subrule (4) the following subrule:\n\n\"(4) Notwithstanding subrule (3), a registered owner or driver\n\nof a bus or caravan of which the glass or other transparent material fitted\n\nto the front side, back side and rear of the bus or caravan is tinted,\n\nsmeared, filmed over, sprayed, pasted, fitted or otherwise treated or\n\ncombined with any material or chemical shall ensure that the\n\ntransmission through the glass or other transparent material is at least\n\nseventy percent visible light.\".\n\nAmendment of rule 9"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 4"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 5,
    "text": {
     "en": "5. Rule 9 of the principal Rules is amended by substituting for subrule (1) the\n\nfollowing subrule:\n\n\"(1) If an inspection carried out by an authorised officer reveals that the\n\nrequirements of subrule 5(1), 5(3) or 5(4) are not complied with, the authorised\n\nofficer shall issue a test certificate in the form as may be determined by the\n\nMinister.\".\n\nSubstitution of rule 10"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 5"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 6,
    "text": {
     "en": "6. The principal Rules are amended by substituting for rule 10 the following rule:\n\n\"Penalty 10. A registered owner or driver of a motor vehicle who fails to\n\ncomply with these Rules commits an offence and shall, in the case of a\n\nfirst conviction, be liable to a fine not exceeding two thousand ringgit\n\nor to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months and in the\n\ncase of a second or subsequent conviction, to a fine not exceeding\n\nfour thousand ringgit or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding\n\ntwelve months or to both.\".\n\nAmendment of Third Schedule"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 6"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 7,
    "text": {
     "en": "7. The Third Schedule to the principal Rules is amended by substituting for\n\nparagraph 13 the following paragraph:\n\n\"13. The data in the Pocket PC shall be inserted in the test certificate in the\n\nform as may be determined by the Minister.\".\n\nDeletion of Fourth Schedule"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 7"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 8,
    "text": {
     "en": "8. The principal Rules are amended by deleting the Fourth Schedule.\n\nMade 28 January 2016\n\n[KP/BD/PJ 0.4/1 Jld. 28(3); PN(PU2)460/LXXXII]\n\nDATO' SRI LIOW TIONG LAI\n\nMinister of Transport"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 8"
    }
   }
  ]
 },
