 "MY-H4941": {
  "lawId": "MY-H4941",
  "sourceLang": "ms",
  "targetLang": "en",
  "engine": "official-extract",
  "model": null,
  "promptVersion": null,
  "translatedAt": "2026-10-28",
  "reviewed": "official",
  "note": "公报原生英文版（与马来文版同一公报并置），逐字照录，非机译。",
  "articles": [
   {
    "no": 1,
    "text": {
     "en": "1. (1) This order may be cited as the Income Tax (Exemption) (No. 5)\nOrder 2018.\n\n (2) This Order comes into operation from the year of assessment 2018 until\nthe year of assessment 2020.\n\nInterpretation"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 1"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 2,
    "text": {
     "en": "2.  In this Order,—\n\n \"Securities Commission  Malaysia\" means the Securities Commission Malaysia\nestablished under the Securities Commission Malaysia Act 1993 [Act 498];\n\n\"company\" means a fund management company which is—\n\n(a) resident in Malaysia;\n\n(b) incorporated under the Companies Act 2016 [Act 777]; and\n\n(c) licensed under the Capital Markets and Services Act 2007 [Act 671 ] or\nregistered with the Securities Commission  Malaysia as a venture capital\nmanagement corporation or a private equity management corporation.\n\nExemption"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 2"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 3,
    "text": {
     "en": "3.  (1)  Subject to subparagraph (2), t he Minister exempts a company from the\npayment of income tax in a basis period for a year of assessment in respect of the\nstatutory income derived from a business of providing fund management services for\nSustainable and Responsible Investment Fund in Malaysia.\n\n(2)  The Sustainable and Responsible Investment F und referred to in\nsubparagraph (1) shall fulfil the requirements set out in the guidelines relating to\nSustainable and Responsible Investment F und issued by the Securities Commission\nMalaysia under the Capital Markets and Services Act 2007.\n\n(3)  Nothing in subparagraph (1) shall absolve or be deemed to have absolved\nthe company from complying with any requirement to submit any return or statement of\naccounts or to furnish any other information under the provisions of the Act.\n\nSeparate account"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 3"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 4,
    "text": {
     "en": "4.  The company shall maintain a separate acco unt for the income derived from the\nbusiness referred to in subparagraph 3(1) for the basis period for each year of\nassessment and that income shall be treated as a separate and distinct source of business\nfor the company.\n\nApplication of paragraphs 5 and 6 of Schedule 7A of the Act"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 4"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 5,
    "text": {
     "en": "5.  Paragraphs 5 and 6 of Schedule 7A to the Act shall apply, mutatis mutandis, to the\namount of statutory income exempted under subparagraph 3(1).\n\nNon-application"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 5"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 6,
    "text": {
     "en": "6.  This Order shall not apply to a company if in the basis period for a year of\nassessment—\n\n(a) the company has been granted any incentive under section 60 G of the Act;\nor\n\n(b) the company has been granted any exemption under paragraph 127(3)(b)\nof the Act.\n\nMade 21 December 2018\n[Perb. CR(8.09)681/2-61(SJ.18)JLD.16(SK.27) ; LHDN.AY.A.600-12/1/7(20)); PN(PU2)80/XCII]\n\nLIM GUAN ENG\nMinister of Finance\n\n[To be laid before the Dewan Rakyat pursuant to subsection 127(4) of the\nIncome Tax Act 1967]"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 6"
    }
   }
  ]
 },
