 "MY-H5222": {
  "lawId": "MY-H5222",
  "sourceLang": "ms",
  "targetLang": "en",
  "engine": "official-extract",
  "model": null,
  "promptVersion": null,
  "translatedAt": "2026-10-28",
  "reviewed": "official",
  "note": "公报原生英文版（与马来文版同一公报并置），逐字照录，非机译。",
  "articles": [
   {
    "no": 1,
    "text": {
     "en": "1. (1) This order may be cited as the Financial Services (Prescribed Qualified\nFinancial Agreement) Order 2023.\n\n (2) This Order comes into operation on 18 December 2023.\n\nInterpretation"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 1"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 2,
    "text": {
     "en": "2. In this Order—\n\n\"asset\" means commodity or any other property , whether tangible or intangible,\nthat is recogni zed by Shariah  as valuable, identifiable, deliverable, and is already in\nexistence and owned by the seller;\n\n\"collateralised Murabahah\" means Shariah compliant transactions which\ncomprise─\n\n(a) sale and purchase of an asset by a seller to a purchaser on a deferred\npayment term where the acquisition cost and the profit are disclosed to\nthe purchaser before or at the time of entering into the sale and purchase\ntransaction; and\n\n(b) any agreement or arrangement which serves as financial collateral\nto secure the payment obligation arising from a transaction of sale and\npurchase of an asset under paragraph (a);\n\n\"netting provision\" means a provision in an agreement which provides that upon\nthe occurrence of the events specified by the parties in the agreement, all obligations\nowed by one party to another party under all transactions are reduced to or replaced with\na single net amount in accordance with the agreement;\n\n\"Shariah compliant transaction\" means a transaction that complies with any ruling\nof the Shariah Advisory Council established under section 51 of the Central Bank of\nMalaysia Act 2009 [Act 701].\n\nPrescribed qualified financial agreement"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 2"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 3,
    "text": {
     "en": "3. An agreement or a set of agreement s with a netting provision  in respect of\ncollateralised Murabahah is prescribed as a qualified financial agreement.\n\nMade 24 November 2023\n[BNM/JUN/1119/11/169; PN(PU2)717/JLD. 7]\n\nSHAIK ABDUL RASHEED BIN ABDUL GHAFFOUR\nGovernor\nCentral Bank of Malaysia\n\nConcurred 29 November 2023\n[BNM/JUN/1119/11/169; PN(PU2)717/JLD. 7]\n\nANWAR BIN IBRAHIM\nMinister of Finance"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 3"
    }
   }
  ]
 },
