 "MY-H5308": {
  "lawId": "MY-H5308",
  "sourceLang": "ms",
  "targetLang": "en",
  "engine": "official-extract",
  "model": null,
  "promptVersion": null,
  "translatedAt": "2026-10-28",
  "reviewed": "official",
  "note": "公报原生英文版（与马来文版同一公报并置），逐字照录，非机译。",
  "articles": [
   {
    "no": 1,
    "text": {
     "en": "1. (1) These regulations may be cited as the Companies (Prescribed Interest for\nIslamic Securities Selling and Buying Negotiated Transaction) Regulations 2017.\n\n(2) These Regulations come into operation on 12 December 2017.\n\nPrescribed interest"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 1"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 2,
    "text": {
     "en": "2. (1) An  interest in a share  of  any  person  under  subsection  8(6)  of  the Act\narising from an Islamic securities selling and buying negotiated transaction is a\nprescribed interest referred to in paragraph 8(9)(d) of the Act.\n\n (2) For the purpose of this regulation—\n\n \"Islamic securities selling and buying negotiated transaction\" has the meaning\nassigned to it in the  rules made by an approved clearing house as approved by the\nSecurities Commission under section 9 of the Capital Market and Services Act 2007\n[Act 671];\n\n \"person\" means—\n\n(a) a supplier in an Islamic securities selling and buying negotiated transaction;\nor\n\n(b) a user in an Islamic securities selling and buying negotiated transaction\nwho keeps the transacted Islamic securiti es for a period of not more than\nthree business days.\n\nMade 11 December 2017\n[KPDNKK 600-1/2/33; PN(PU2)740]\n\nDATO' SERI HAMZAH BIN ZAINUDIN\nMinister of Domestic Trade,\nCo-operatives and Consumerism"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 2"
    }
   }
  ]
 },
