 "MY-H5562": {
  "lawId": "MY-H5562",
  "sourceLang": "ms",
  "targetLang": "en",
  "engine": "official-extract",
  "model": null,
  "promptVersion": null,
  "translatedAt": "2026-10-28",
  "reviewed": "official",
  "note": "公报原生英文版（与马来文版同一公报并置），逐字照录，非机译。",
  "articles": [
   {
    "no": 1,
    "text": {
     "en": "1. (1) This order may be cited as the Passports (Exemption of Visa to Expatriate\nWho is Citizen of India) Order 2019.\n\n(2) This O rder has effect for the period from 1 January 201 9\nto 31 December 2019.\n\nExemption"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 1"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 2,
    "text": {
     "en": "2. The Minister exempts an expatriate who is a  citizen of India and working outside\nIndia except in Singapore from the requirement of visa under subsection 2(1) of the Act\nsubject to the following conditions:\n\n(a) the expatriate shall be registered in the  electronic travel registration and\ninformation system provided by the Director General an d the registration\nmay be made—\n\n(i) by the expatriate himself; or\n\n(ii) on behalf of the expatriate, by  a travel agency in India which is\nregistered with the Malaysian Mission Office in India;\n\n(b) the expatriate shall travel to Malaysia within three months after he is\nregistered in the electronic travel registration and information system;\n\n(c) the period of visit of the expatriate is limited to fifteen days only and shall\nnot be extended;\n\n(d) the expatriate shall enter and exit from Malaysia only through the authorized\nairports as gazetted under subsection 5(1) of the  Immigration Act 1959/63\n[Act 155] or through immigration control posts as follows:\n\n(i)  D11 Sultan Iskandar Building, Johore;\n\n(ii) D12A Immigration Control Post at Kompleks Sultan Abu Bakar,\nTanjung Kupang, Johore;\n\n(iii) D01 Padang Besar, Perlis;\n\n(iv) D06 Bukit Kayu Itam, Changloon, Kedah;\n\n(v)  D20 Sungai Tujoh, Miri, Sarawak; or\n\n(vi) D22A Immigration Control P ost Tedungan, District of Batu Danau\nLimbang, 5th Division, Sarawak;\n\n(e) the expatriate is not allowed to apply for any other p asses under the\nImmigration Regulations 1963 [L.N. 228/1963];\n\n(f) the expatriate shall have a travel air ticket back  direct to India or a travel air\nticket to any country if the expatriate travels by air;\n\n(g) the expatriate shall produce work information, in business, professional or\ntechnical field, and a long term pass from any country where the\nexpatriate works;\n\n(h) the expatriate shall, on arrival,  produce a proof that he has  sufficient\npocket-money, credit card  or bank card, and produce his  itinerary in\nMalaysia; and\n\n(i) the expatriate is allowed to re -register as in subparagraph  (a) to\nenter Malaysia after the period of three months from the date he\nleaves Malaysia.\n\nMade 2 January 2019\n[KDN.IM.S.600-1/3/30 JLD 8; PN(PU2)482/II]\n\n  TAN SRI DATO' HAJI MUHYIDDIN BIN HAJI MOHD YASSIN\n                           Minister of Home Affairs"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 2"
    }
   }
  ]
 },
