 "MY-H5588": {
  "lawId": "MY-H5588",
  "sourceLang": "ms",
  "targetLang": "en",
  "engine": "official-extract",
  "model": null,
  "promptVersion": null,
  "translatedAt": "2026-10-28",
  "reviewed": "official",
  "note": "公报原生英文版（与马来文版同一公报并置），逐字照录，非机译。",
  "articles": [
   {
    "no": 1,
    "text": {
     "en": "1. (1) These regulations may be cited as the Prevention and Control of Infectious\n\nDiseases (Fee for Coronavirus Disease 2019 (COVID-19) Detection Test)\n\n(Amendment) (No. 2) Regulations 2020.\n\n(2) These Regulations come into operation on 1 January 2021.\n\nAmendment of regulation 2"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 1"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 2,
    "text": {
     "en": "2. The Prevention and Control of Infectious Diseases (Fee for Coronavirus\n\nDisease 2019 (COVID-19) Detection Test) Regulations 2020 [P.U. (A) 190/2020],\n\nwhich are referred to as the \"principal Regulations\" in these Regulations, are amended\n\nin regulation 2 by substituting for subregulation (1) the following subregulation:\n\n\"(1) In these Regulations—\n\n\"COVID-19\" means Coronavirus Disease 2019 (COVID-19);\n\n\"foreign employee\" means a holder of a Visit Pass\n\n(Temporary Employment) issued under regulation 11 of the Immigration\n\nRegulations 1963 [F.L.N. 228/1963].\".\n\nAmendment of regulation 3"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 2"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 3,
    "text": {
     "en": "3. Regulation 3 of the principal Regulations is amended—\n\n(a) in subregulation (2), by substituting for the words \"as determined by the\n\nDirector General\" the words \"managed by the Government\"; and\n\n(b) by inserting after subregulation (2) the following subregulation:\n\n\"(3) If an employer who employs a foreign employee is instructed\n\nby an authorized officer to cause his foreign employee to undergo\n\nCOVID-19 detection test and the employer chooses that his foreign\n\nemployee undergoes the test at any Government hospital or any place\n\nmanaged by the Government to be a place to undergo COVID-19\n\ndetection test, the employer of such foreign employee shall pay the fee\n\nspecified in column (3) of the Schedule in relation to the type of\n\nCOVID-19 detection test specified in column (1) as determined\n\nunder regulation 4.\".\n\nNew regulations 6 and 7"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 3"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 4,
    "text": {
     "en": "4. The principal Regulations are amended by inserting after regulation 5 the following\n\nregulations:\n\n\"Offence"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 4"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 6,
    "text": {
     "en": "6. Any person who contravenes regulation 3 commits an offence and\n\nshall, on conviction, be liable to a fine not exceeding one thousand ringgit\n\nor to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months or to both.\n\n Recovery of fee as civil debt"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 6"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 7,
    "text": {
     "en": "7. (1) Any fee due from and payable by any person\n\nunder regulation 3 may be recovered as a civil debt due to the Government.\n\n(2) Notwithstanding the conviction of any person\n\nunder regulation 6, any fee due from and payable by that person\n\nunder regulation 3 may be recovered as a civil debt due\n\nto the Government.\".\n\nMade 31 December 2020\n\n [KKM.600-29/4/146 Jld.2; PN(PU2)470/IV]\n\nDATO' SRI DR. ADHAM BIN BABA\n\nMinister of Health"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 7"
    }
   }
  ]
 },
