 "MY-H5688": {
  "lawId": "MY-H5688",
  "sourceLang": "ms",
  "targetLang": "en",
  "engine": "official-extract",
  "model": null,
  "promptVersion": null,
  "translatedAt": "2026-10-28",
  "reviewed": "official",
  "note": "公报原生英文版（与马来文版同一公报并置），逐字照录，非机译。",
  "articles": [
   {
    "no": 1,
    "text": {
     "en": "1. (1) This order may be cited as the Members of Parliament (Remuneration)\n(Amendment of First Schedule) Order 2000.\n\n(2) This Order shall be deemed to have come into operation on 5 April\n\nP.U. (A) 410.\n\nAmendment of First Schedule"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 1"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 2,
    "text": {
     "en": "2. The Members of Parliament (Remuneration) Act 1980 (Act 237) is amended\nin the First Schedule—\n\n(a) in paragraph 4—\n\n(i) by inserting after subparagraph (1) the following subparagraphs:\n\n\"(1a) Notwithstanding subparagraph (1), a Member who\nceases to hold the office of President of the Senate, or\nSpeaker of the House of Representatives but continues to\nbe a Member of either House of Parliament may be paid\na gratuity calculated under subparagraph (1).\n\n(1B) Notwithstanding subparagraph (1) and subject to\nsubparagraph (1c), a Member of the Administration who\nceases to hold the office of Prime Minister, Deputy Prime\nMinister, Minister, Deputy Minister or Parliamentary\nSecretary and—\n\n(a) continues to be a Member of either House of\nParliament; or\n\n(b) ceases to be a Member of either House of Parliament,\nmay be granted a gratuity calculated on the following formula:\n1/48 x salary x 12 x period of reckonable service\n\n(1c) For the purposes of calculating the gratuity based\non the formula stipulated in subparagraph (1B), \"period of\nreckonable service\" shall be the period of reckonable service\nas a Member up to seventy-two months and if such period\nexceeds seventy-two months, only such period of service\nas a Member of the Administration shall be reckoned.\n\n(1p) If a Member of the Administration has been paid\na gratuity under subparagraph (1) or paragraph 4a, such\ngratuity shall be deducted from the gratuity that falls due\nto be payable to him under subparagraph (1B).\n\n(le) If a gratuity falls due to be payable to a Member\nunder subparagraph (1) or (1A) but that gratuity is less\nthan the gratuity that had been paid to him under\nsubparagraph (1s), the gratuity shall be deemed to have\nbeen paid to such Member for any period of his reckonable\nservice under this Act.\";\n\n(ii) in subparagraph (2), by substituting for the words \"under this\n\nparagraph\" the words \"under subparagraph (1), (1A) or (1s), as\nthe case may be,\";\n\n2869                       P.U. (A) 410-411.\n\n(iii) in subparagraph (3), by substituting for the words \"under this\nparagraph\" the words \"under subparagraph (1), (1A) or (18), as\nthe case may be\"; and\n\n(iv) by deleting subparagraph (4);\n(b) in paragraph 4a—\n\n(i) in subparagraph (1), by deleting the words \"not exceeding 72\nmonths\";\n\n(ii) by inserting after subparagraph (1) the following subparagraph:\n\n\"(1a) For the purposes of calculating the gratuity based\non the formula stipulated in subparagraph (1), \"period of\nreckonable service\" shall be the period of reckonable service\nas a Member up to seventy-two months and if such period\nexceeds seventy-two months, only such period of service\nas a Member of the Administration shall be reckoned.\";\nand\n\n(iii) in subparagraph (3), by inserting after the words \"under this\nparagraph\" the words \"or subparagraph (1) or (1B) of paragraph\n4, as the case may be\"; and\n\n(c) in subparagraphs 5(1) and (2), by inserting after the words \"paragraph\n4\" the words \"or paragraph 4a, as the case may be\".\n\nMade 23 October 2000.\n[JPA/PEN(R) 228/6/6-12; PN(PU?)369/IV]\n\nBy Command,\n\nTan Sri Abdul HALIM BIN ALI\nSecretary to the Cabinet\n\nP.U. (A) 411.\nAKTA PEMBANGUNAN SUMBER MANUSIA 1992\n\nPERINTAH PEMBANGUNAN SUMBER MANUSIA (PENGECUALIAN) 2000\n\nPada menjalankan kuasa yang diberikan oleh seksyen 5 Akta Pembangunan\nSumber Manusia 1992 (Akta 491), Menteri membuat perintah yang berikut:\n\nNama dan permulaan kuat kuasa\n\n1. (1) Perintah ini bolehlah dinamakan Perintah Pembangunan Sumber\nManusia (Pengecualian) 2000.\n\n(2) Perintah ini hendaklah disifatkan telah mula berkuat kuasa pada 1 Januari"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 2"
    }
   }
  ]
 },
