 "MY-H5906": {
  "lawId": "MY-H5906",
  "sourceLang": "ms",
  "targetLang": "en",
  "engine": "official-extract",
  "model": null,
  "promptVersion": null,
  "translatedAt": "2026-10-28",
  "reviewed": "official",
  "note": "公报原生英文版（与马来文版同一公报并置），逐字照录，非机译。",
  "articles": [
   {
    "no": 1,
    "text": {
     "en": "1. (1) These rules may be cited as the Malaysia Deposit Insurance\nCorporation (Return or Interest on an Index -Linked Deposit Held by a\nDeposit-Taking Member) Rules 2012.\n\n(2) These Rules come into operation on 6 December 2012.\n\nInterpretation"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 1"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 2,
    "text": {
     "en": "2. In these Rules―\n\n \"calculation date\" means―\n\n(a) for the purpose of calculating the obligatory payment under section 56  of\nthe Act or discretionary payment under paragraph 62 (b) of the Act,\nthe date of the filing of the petition for the winding up; and\n\n(b) for the purpose of calculating the discretionary payment under paragraph\n62(a) of the Act, the date of the payment by the Corporation.\n\nReturn or interest on index-linked deposit"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 2"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 3,
    "text": {
     "en": "3.  For the purpose of calculating the return or interest for obligatory payment  or\ndiscretionary payment in relation to an index -linked deposit held by a deposit -taking\nmember, such return or interest shall be determined in the following manner:\n\n(a) for an index -linked deposit where the repayment of principal and the\npayment of return or interest is subject to a condition of an event\noccurring or not occurring in the future and the condition has not\nmaterialised as at the calculation d ate, the return or interest shall be\ncalculated as at the calculation date―\n\n(i) based on the Overnight Policy Rate set by Bank Negara Malaysia; or\n\n(ii) at the rate of 6% per annum,\n\nwhichever is lower;\n\n(b) for an index-linked deposit other than that referred to in subrule (a)―\n\n(i) the return or interest shall first be determined based on the\nmark-to-market value of the underlying asset or reference as at the\ncalculation date;\n\n(ii) in the event that the return or interest cannot be calculated based\non the method referred to  in paragraph (b)(i), the alternative\nreference rate or alternative method of calculation as specified in\nthe terms and conditions of the index -linked deposit shall apply as\nat the calculation date; and\n\n(iii) in the event that the return or interest cannot be calculated based\non the methods referred to in paragraph (b)(i) or (b)(ii), the return\nor interest shall be calculated as at the calculation date―\n\n(A) based on the Overnight Policy Rate set by Bank Negara\nMalaysia; or\n\n(B) at the rate of 6% per annum,\n\n   whichever is lower; and\n\n(c) for all types of index -linked deposits, the calculation of return or interest\nshall not take into account any penalties specified in the terms and\nconditions and the early termination clause sh all be deemed exercised on\nthe calculation date.\n\nMade 16 November 2012\n[PIDM/PN/4/2012; PN(PU2)689/II]\n\n     TAN SRI DATUK DR ABDUL SAMAD HAJI ALIAS\n                                   Chairman\n        Malaysia Deposit Insurance Corporation\n\nApproved 26 November 2012\n[PIDM/PN/4/2012; PN(PU2)689/II]\n\n             DATO' SERI AHMAD HUSNI MOHAMAD HANADZLAH\n           Second Minister of Finance"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 3"
    }
   }
  ]
 },
