 "MY-H5933": {
  "lawId": "MY-H5933",
  "sourceLang": "ms",
  "targetLang": "en",
  "engine": "official-extract",
  "model": null,
  "promptVersion": null,
  "translatedAt": "2026-10-28",
  "reviewed": "official",
  "note": "公报原生英文版（与马来文版同一公报并置），逐字照录，非机译。",
  "articles": [
   {
    "no": 1,
    "text": {
     "en": "1. Ordinan ini boleh-lah di-namakan Ordinan No. 60 Nama.\n(Kuasa2 Perlu) Dharurat, 1970.\n\nPU. (A) 438.                 1562\n\nSe ee ee a A an\n\npindaan 2. Sekshen SA dalam Ordinan Perjanjian Bretton Woods,\n\nsekshen 5A. 1957 ada-lah dengan ini di-pinda dengan memasokkan\n\npy   sa-lepas sahaja sekshen-kechil (2) suatu sekshen-kechi\n(3) yang baharu saperti berikut:\n\n\"(3) Bank Negara Malaysia may, with the prior\napproval in writing of the Minister of Finance, accept\non behalf of the Government of Malaysia and pay any\nincrease in the subscription of Malaysia to the Interna-\ntional Monetary Fund which is made in accordance\nwith the provisions of the Fund Agreement.\"\n\nDi-ishtiharkan di-Istana Negara, Kuala Lumpur, pada\n12 haribulan November, 1970.          '\n\nIMGN. (PA) R. 21.11/Jld. 7 (23)]\n\nTUANKU ABDUL HALIM MU‘ADZAM SHAH,\nYang di-Pertuan Agong\n\nLAWS OF MALAYSIA\nOrdinance 60\n\nEMERGENCY (ESSENTIAL POWERS)\nORDINANCE No. 60, 1970\n\nAn Ordinance promulgated by the Yang di-Pertuan Agong\nunder Article 150 (2) of the Federal Constitution.\n\n[3rd December, 1970.]\n\nWHEREAS by reason of the existence of a grave emergency\npu.(A). threatening the security of Malaysia, a Proclamation of\n145/69. Emergency has been issued by the Yang di-Pertuan Agong\n\nunder Article 150 of the Constitution;\n\nP.U.(A)       AND WHEREAS Parliament was dissolved on the twentieth\n94/69.       day of March, 1969, and has not been summoned to meet;\n\nAND WHEREAS the Yang di-Pertuan Agong is satisfied that\nF.M.75/57. jmmediate action is required to amend the Bretton Woods\nAgreement Ordinance, 1957;\n\nIT IS HEREBY ENACTED by the Duli Yang Maha\nMulia Seri Paduka Baginda Yang di-Pertuan Agong\npursuant to Clause (2) of Article 150 of the Constitution as\nfollows :\n\nCitation. 1, This Ordinance may be cited as the Emergency (Essential\nPowers) Ordinance No. 60, 1970.\n\n1563             P.U. (A) 438-439."
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 1"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 2,
    "text": {
     "en": "2. Section 5A of the Bretton Woods Agreement Ordinance, Amendment\n1957, is hereby amended by inserting immediately after sub- 21 **\"on\nsection (2) thereof a new sub-section (3) as follows :     F.M.75/57.\n\n\"(3) Bank Negara Malaysia may, with the prior\napproval in writing of the Minister of Finance, accept\non behalf of the Government of Malaysia and pay any\nincrease in the subscription of Malaysia to the Interna-\ntional Monetary Fund which is made in accordance\nwith the provisions of the Fund Agreement.\"\n\nPromulgated at the Istana Negara, Kuala Lumpur, on the\n12th day of November, 1970.\n\n[MGN. (PA) R. 21.11/Jld. 7 (23).]\n\nTUANKU ABDUL HALIM MU‘ADZAM SHAH,\nYang di-Pertuan Agong\n\nP.U. (A) 439.\nAKTA KASTAM. 1967\n\n(No. 62 tahun 1967)\n\nPADA menjalankan kuasa? yang di-beri oleh sekshen 12 Akta Kastam,\n1967, Mentri Kewangan dengan ini membuat Perentah yang berikut:"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 2"
    }
   }
  ]
 },
