 "MY-H6196": {
  "lawId": "MY-H6196",
  "sourceLang": "ms",
  "targetLang": "en",
  "engine": "official-extract",
  "model": null,
  "promptVersion": null,
  "translatedAt": "2026-10-28",
  "reviewed": "official",
  "note": "公报原生英文版（与马来文版同一公报并置），逐字照录，非机译。",
  "articles": [
   {
    "no": 1,
    "text": {
     "en": "1. These regulations may be cited as the Fire Services (Compounding of Offences)\n\n(Amendment) Regulations 2026.\n\nAmendment of regulation 7"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 1"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 2,
    "text": {
     "en": "2. The Fire Services (Compounding of Offences) Regulations 2000\n\n[P.U. (A) 313/2000], which are referred to as the \"principal Regulations\" in these\n\nRegulations, are amended in regulation 7—\n\n(a) by substituting for subregulation (1) the following subregulation:\n\n\"(1) A person who accepts an offer to compound an offence shall\n\npay the amount specified in the notice of offer—\n\n(a) in cash and shall be delivered personally to the\n\nDirector General or any Fire Officer authorized by\n\nhim in writing;\n\n(b) by money order, postal order, cashier's order,\n\nbanker's cheque or bank draft made payable to the\n\nDirector General of Fire and Rescue Department and\n\ncrossed with the words \"Account Payee Only\" and\n\nshall be delivered personally or sent by registered\n\npost to the Director General of Fire and Rescue\n\nDepartment to the address at Jabatan Bomba dan\n\nPenyelamat Malaysia, Lebuh Wawasan, Presint 7,\n\n62250 Putrajaya; or\n\n(c) through credit card, debit card, charge card, prepaid\n\ncard or any other forms of electronic fund transfer\n\ninto the account of Fire and Rescue Department of\n\nMalaysia.\"; and\n\n(b) by deleting subregulations (2) and (3).\n\nAmendment of Schedule"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 2"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 3,
    "text": {
     "en": "3. The principal Regulations are amended in the Schedule—\n\n(a) by substituting for the words \"If you accept this offer, payment shall be\n\nmade in cash or by money order, postal order, cashier's order,\n\nbanker's cheque or bank draft made payable to the Director General,\n\nFire and Rescue Department and crossed with the words\n\n\"Account Payee Only\".\" the following words:\n\n\"If you accept this offer, payment shall be made—\n\n(a) in cash and shall be delivered personally to the Director\n\nGeneral or any Fire Officer authorized by him in writing;\n\n(b) by money order, postal order, cashier's order,\n\nbanker's cheque or bank draft made payable to the\n\nDirector General of Fire and Rescue Department and crossed\n\nwith the words \"Account Payee Only\" and shall be delivered\n\npersonally or sent by registered post to the Director General\n\nof Fire and Rescue Department to the address at\n\nJabatan Bomba dan Penyelamat Malaysia, Lebuh Wawasan,\n\nPresint 7, 62250 Putrajaya; or\n\n(c) through credit card, debit card, charge card, prepaid card or\n\nany other forms of electronic fund transfer into\n\nthe account of Fire and Rescue Department of Malaysia.\"; and\n\n(b) by substituting for the words \"I enclose herewith *cash/\n\nmoney order/postal order/cashier's order/banker's cheque/bank draft\n\nNo. ………….…\" the words \"I enclosed herewith the payment in *cash/\n\nmoney order/postal order/cashier's order/banker's cheque/bank draft\n\nno. …………………….. made payable to the Director General of the\n\nFire and Rescue Department and crossed with the words\n\n\"Account Payee Only\"/proof of payment through *credit card/debit\n\ncard/charge card/prepaid card/other electronic fund transfer\".\n\nMade 30 January 2026\n\n[KPKT(2)12/840/4; PN(PU2)471/JLD.7]\n\nNGA KOR MING\n\nMinister of Housing and Local Government"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 3"
    }
   }
  ]
 },
 "MY-H6197": {
  "lawId": "MY-H6197",
  "sourceLang": "ms",
  "targetLang": "en",
  "engine": "official-extract",
  "model": null,
  "promptVersion": null,
  "translatedAt": "2026-10-28",
  "reviewed": "official",
  "note": "公报原生英文版（与马来文版同一公报并置），逐字照录，非机译。",
  "articles": [
   {
    "no": 1,
    "text": {
     "en": "1. (1) These regulations may be cited as the Capital Markets and Services\n(Capital Market Compensation Fund) Regulations 2012.\n\n (2) These Regulations come into operation on 28 December 2012.\n\nApplication"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 1"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 2,
    "text": {
     "en": "2.  These Regulations shall apply to the Capital Market Compensation Fund\nCorporation and the Capital Market Compensation Fund established under Part IV\nof the Act.\n\nInterpretation"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 2"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 3,
    "text": {
     "en": "3. In these Regulations―\n\n\"Fund\" means the Capital Market Compensation Fund;\n\n\"Corporation\" means the Capital Market Compensation Fund Corporation.\n\nInvestment of monies in the Fund"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 3"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 4,
    "text": {
     "en": "4. The Corporation may invest any monies which forms part of the Fund and is not\nimmediately required for any other purposes under Part IV of the Act—\n\n(a) in fixed deposits or any other type of investments or placements with a\nlicensed institution;\n(b) in a unit trust scheme approved by the Commission; or\n\n(c) in any other type of investment subject to the Corporation obtaining the\nprior approval of the Commission and subject to any terms and conditions\nas may be specified by the Commission.\n\nRegulatory report to the Commission"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 4"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 5,
    "text": {
     "en": "5.  Within three months after the end of each financial year, the Corporation shall\nprepare and submit a regulatory report to the Commission in writing, of the following:\n\n(a) where the Corporation invest any monies which forms part of the Fund―\n\n(i) the particulars of the licensed institution in which the fixed deposit\nor any other type of investment or placement is made;\n\n(ii) the relevant rate or rates of interest paid on the fixed deposit or\nthe investment or placement for that financial year;\n\n(iii) the total amount of i nterest or profit earned from the fixed deposit\nor investment or placement for that financial year;\n\n(iv) the manner and time of payment of such interest, profit or other\nform of income;\n\n(v) the securities in which the Corporation has invested;\n\n(vi) the appreciation or depreciation in value of investments held;\n\n(vii) dividends declared and paid in respect of those securities; and\n\n(b) the amount to be charged to meet the expenses incurred or involved in\nthe administration of the Fund.\n\nAppeal to the Commission"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 5"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 6,
    "text": {
     "en": "6.  (1) The Commission shall determine its own procedures in hearing any\nappeals made to it pursuant to section 166 of the Act.\n\n (2)  The Commission may in respect of an appeal under subregulation (1)—\n\n(a)  affirm the determination of the Corporation;\n\n(b)  set aside the determination of the Corporation; or\n\n(c) substitute the determination of the Corporation with its own\ndetermination.\n\nMade 24 December 2012\n[RS(A&R)/CF-CMFC.1/11(016)-1; PN(PU2)662/VII]\n\n        RANJIT AJIT SINGH\n       Chairman Securities Commission\n\nApproved 27 December 2012\n[KK/BPKA/K1/(S)/483/128/1/1 Jld.8; PN(PU2)662/VII]\n\n                 DATO' SERI AHMAD HUSNI MOHAMAD HANADZLAH\n                  Second Minister of Finance"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 6"
    }
   }
  ]
 },
