 "MY-H6271": {
  "lawId": "MY-H6271",
  "sourceLang": "ms",
  "targetLang": "en",
  "engine": "official-extract",
  "model": null,
  "promptVersion": null,
  "translatedAt": "2026-10-28",
  "reviewed": "official",
  "note": "公报原生英文版（与马来文版同一公报并置），逐字照录，非机译。",
  "articles": [
   {
    "no": 1,
    "text": {
     "en": "1. (1) This order may be cited as the Passports (Exemption of Visa to Tourist\n\nWho is Citizen of India) Order 2019.\n\n(2) This Order has effect for the period from 1 January 2019\n\nto 31 December 2019.\n\nExemption"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 1"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 2,
    "text": {
     "en": "2. The Minister exempts a tourist who is a citizen of India from the requirement of\n\nvisa under subsection 2(1) of the Act subject to the following conditions:\n\n(a) the tourist shall be registered in the electronic travel registration and\n\ninformation system provided by the Director General and the registration\n\nmay be made—\n\n(i) by the tourist himself; or\n\n(ii) on behalf of the tourist, by a travel agency in India which is registered\n\nwith the Malaysian Mission Office in India;\n\n(b) the tourist shall travel to Malaysia within three months after he is registered\n\nin the electronic travel registration and information system;\n\n(c) the period of visit of the tourist is limited to fifteen days only and shall not be\n\nextended;\n\n(d) the tourist shall enter and exit from Malaysia only through the authorized\n\nairports as gazetted under subsection 5(1) of the Immigration Act 1959/63\n\n[Act 155] or through immigration control posts as follows:\n\n(i) D11 Sultan Iskandar Building, Johore;\n\n(ii) D12A Immigration Control Post at Kompleks Sultan Abu Bakar,\n\nTanjung Kupang, Johore;\n\n(iii) D01 Padang Besar, Perlis;\n\n(iv) D06 Bukit Kayu Itam, Changloon, Kedah;\n\n(v) D20 Sungai Tujoh, Miri, Sarawak; or\n\n(vi) D22A Immigration Control Post Tedungan, District of Batu Danau\n\nLimbang, 5th Division, Sarawak;\n\n(e) the tourist is not allowed to apply for any other passes under the\n\nImmigration Regulations 1963 [L.N. 228/1963];\n\n(f) the tourist shall have a travel air ticket back direct to India or a travel air\n\nticket to any country if the tourist travels by air;\n\n(g) the tourist shall, on arrival, produce proof of sufficient pocket-money,\n\ncredit card or bank card and produce his itinerary in Malaysia; and\n\n(h) the tourist is allowed to re-register as in subparagraph (a) to enter Malaysia\n\nafter the period of three months from the date he leaves Malaysia.\n\nMade 2 January 2019\n\n[KDN.IM.S.600-1/3/30 JLD 8; PN(PU2)482/II]\n\nTAN SRI DATO' HAJI MUHYIDDIN BIN HAJI MOHD YASSIN\n\n Minister of Home Affairs"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 2"
    }
   }
  ]
 },
