 "MY-H6299": {
  "lawId": "MY-H6299",
  "sourceLang": "ms",
  "targetLang": "en",
  "engine": "official-extract",
  "model": null,
  "promptVersion": null,
  "translatedAt": "2026-10-28",
  "reviewed": "official",
  "note": "公报原生英文版（与马来文版同一公报并置），逐字照录，非机译。",
  "articles": [
   {
    "no": 1,
    "text": {
     "en": "1. (1) This order may be cited as the Federal Roads (Private Management)\n\n(Collection of Tolls) (Malaysia-Singapore Second Crossing Bridge and Expressway\n\nand Perling Expressway) (Amendment) Order 2026.\n\n(2) This Order comes into operation on 6 February 2026.\n\nSubstitution of paragraph 3"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 1"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 2,
    "text": {
     "en": "2. The Federal Roads (Private Management) (Collection of Tolls) (Malaysia\u0002Singapore Second Crossing Bridge and Expressway and Perling Expressway) Order 1998\n\n[P.U. (A) 97/1998] is amended by substituting for paragraph 3 the following paragraph:\n\n\"Payment of toll. 3. (1) A driver of a vehicle who uses—\n\n(a) a valid debit card, credit card or\n\nprepaid card;\n\n(b) an electronic device with a valid\n\nprepaid card;\n\n(c) a valid electronic sticker which has\n\nbeen installed on the windscreen,\n\nheadlamp of the vehicle or on any\n\nother parts of the vehicle which has\n\nbeen determined for its installation;\n\nor\n\n(d) an application for Automatic Number\n\nPlate Recognition System,\n\nshall pay the amount of toll payable under\n\nsubparagraph 2(1) when passing through a dedicated\n\ntoll lane at the following toll plaza:\n\n(a) Toll Plaza A at Level 0 of Sultan Abu\n\nBakar Complex situated at kilometre\n\n4.96 (distance as measured in a\n\nnortherly direction from the\n\ninternational boundary of Malaysia\n\nand Singapore with reference to\n\nSingapore Cassini Grid at coordinate\n\nN+36978.189 and E+5732.504);\n\n(b) Tanjung Kupang Toll Plaza situated at\n\nkilometre 5.76 (distance as measured\n\nin a northerly direction from the\n\ninternational boundary of Malaysia\n\nand Singapore with reference to\n\nSingapore Cassini Grid at coordinate\n\nN+36978.189 and E+5732.504);\n\n(c) Lima Kedai Toll Plaza situated at\n\nkilometre 20.72 (distance as\n\nmeasured in a northerly direction\n\nfrom the international boundary of\n\nMalaysia and Singapore with\n\nreference to Singapore Cassini Grid at\n\ncoordinate N+36978.189 and\n\nE+5732.504); or\n\n(d) Perling Toll Plaza situated at\n\nkilometre 24.65 (distance as\n\nmeasured in a northerly direction\n\nfrom the international boundary of\n\nMalaysia and Singapore with\n\nreference to Singapore Cassini Grid at\n\ncoordinate N+36978.189 and\n\nE+5732.504),\n\nas shown on the map in the Third Schedule and Fourth\n\nSchedule.\n\n(2) For the purpose of payment of toll under\n\nsubparagraph (1), a driver of a vehicle shall—\n\n(a) touch the valid debit card, credit card\n\nor prepaid card on the electronic\n\nmachine reader;\n\n(b) display the electronic device with\n\na valid prepaid card;\n\n(c) display a valid electronic sticker\n\nwhich has been installed on the\n\nwindscreen, headlamp of the vehicle\n\nor on any other parts of the vehicle\n\nwhich has been determined for its\n\ninstallation; or\n\n(d) display a valid vehicle registration\n\nnumber plate in accordance with\n\nthe applicable laws and ensure\n\nthe vehicle registration number is\n\nregistered with a valid open payment\n\napplication with a valid and active\n\nmode of payment.\n\n(3) A driver of a vehicle who uses a debit card,\n\na credit card, a prepaid card, an electronic device with\n\nprepaid card, an electronic sticker or an application for\n\nAutomatic Number Plate Recognition System shall ensure\n\nmoney in the debit card, credit card, prepaid card,\n\nelectronic device with prepaid card, electronic sticker or\n\napplication for Automatic Number Plate Recognition\n\nSystem is sufficient for the purpose of payment of toll.\n\n(4) The electronic sticker which has been\n\ninstalled for the purpose of subparagraph (1) shall not be\n\ntransferred or moved to another vehicle in any manner\n\nwhatsoever.\n\n(5) A driver of a vehicle who has installed a\n\nvalid electronic sticker shall not do or cause to be done\n\nany modification to the electronic sticker or any act which\n\nmay interfere with the function of the electronic sticker.\n\n(6) \"Prepaid card\", \"electronic device with\n\nprepaid card\" or \"electronic sticker\" referred to in this\n\nparagraph means a prepaid card, an electronic device\n\nwith prepaid card or an electronic sticker as approved by\n\nthe Minister and issued for the purpose of payment\n\nof toll.\".\n\nMade 29 January 2026\n\n[KKR.PUU.110-1/7/43; PN(PU2)426/JLD.74]\n\nDATO SRI ALEXANDER NANTA LINGGI\n\nMinister of Works"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 2"
    }
   }
  ]
 },
