 "MY-H6919": {
  "lawId": "MY-H6919",
  "sourceLang": "ms",
  "targetLang": "en",
  "engine": "official-extract",
  "model": null,
  "promptVersion": null,
  "translatedAt": "2026-10-28",
  "reviewed": "official",
  "note": "公报原生英文版（与马来文版同一公报并置），逐字照录，非机译。",
  "articles": [
   {
    "no": 1,
    "text": {
     "en": "1.  (1)   This order may be cited as the  Income Tax (Exemption) (No. 2)\nOrder 2016.\n\n(2)  This Order has effect from the year of assessment 2016.\n\nApplication"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 1"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 2,
    "text": {
     "en": "2. This Order shall apply to sukuk wakala with the nominal value  up to one billion\nand five hundred million  United States Dollar  (US$1,500,000,000.00), other than\nconvertible loan stock , issued by the Malaysia Sukuk Global Berhad\n(formerly known as 1Malaysia Sukuk Global Berhad).\n\nExemption"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 2"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 3,
    "text": {
     "en": "3. (1) The Minister exempts any person from the payment of income tax in the\nbasis period for each year of assessment in relation to gains or profits derived, in lieu of\ninterest, from the sukuk wakala in accordance with the principle of Wakala.\n\n(2) Nothing in subparagraph (1) shall absolve or is deemed to have absolved\nthe person from complying with any requirement to submit any return or statement of\naccounts or to furnish any other information under the Act.\n\nNon-application"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 3"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 4,
    "text": {
     "en": "4. Section 109 of the Act shall not apply to the income exempted under this Order.\n\nMade 7 April 2016\n[KK/BFE/FIS (S) 10/824/2 Jld. 3; PN(PU2)80/LXXX]\n\nDATO' SERI AHMAD HUSNI BIN MOHAMAD HANADZLAH\nSecond Minister of Finance\n\n[To be laid before the Dewan Rakyat pursuant to subsection 127(4) of the\nIncome Tax Act 1967]"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 4"
    }
   }
  ]
 },
