 "MY-H6977": {
  "lawId": "MY-H6977",
  "sourceLang": "ms",
  "targetLang": "en",
  "engine": "official-extract",
  "model": null,
  "promptVersion": null,
  "translatedAt": "2026-10-28",
  "reviewed": "official",
  "note": "公报原生英文版（与马来文版同一公报并置），逐字照录，非机译。",
  "articles": [
   {
    "no": 1,
    "text": {
     "en": "1. (1) This order  may be cited as the Passports (Exemption of Visa to\nExpatriate Who is Citizen of India) Order 2017.\n\n(2) This Order has effect for the period from 1 April 2017 to 31 March 2018.\n\nExemption"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 1"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 2,
    "text": {
     "en": "2. The Minister exempts an expatriate who is a citizen of India and working outside\nIndia except in Singapore from the requirement of visa under  subsection 2(1) of the Act\nsubject to the following conditions:\n\n(a) the expatriate shall be registered in the electronic travel registration and\ninformation system and the registration may be made—\n\n(i) by the expatriate himself; or\n\n(ii) on behalf of the expatriate, by a travel agency which is  registered\n  with the Malaysian Mission Office abroad;\n\n(b) the expatriate shall travel to Malaysia within three months after he is\nregistered in the electronic travel registration and information system;\n\n(c) the period of visit of the expatriate is limited to fifteen days only and shall\nnot be extended;\n\n(d)  the expatriate shall enter a nd exit from Malaysia only through authorized\npoints of entry as follows:\n\n(i) by air—\n\n(A)  U21A Kuala Lumpur International Airport, Sepang;\n\n(B)  U05 Pulau Pinang Airport, Bayan Lepas, Penang;\n\n(C)  U15 Sultan Ismail Airport, Johor Bahru, Johore;\n\n(D)  U17 Kuching Airport, First Division, Sarawak;\n\n(E)  U29 Kota Kinabalu Airport, Sabah;\n\n(F)  U02 Langkawi International Airport, Kedah;\n\n(G)  U14 Melaka Airport, Batu Berendam, Malacca;\n\n(H)  U16 Labuan Airport, Federal Territory; or\n\n(I)       U23 Miri Airport, Fourth Division, Sarawak; or\n\n(ii) by land—\n\n(A)  D11 Sultan Iskandar Building, Johore;\n\n(B) D12A Immigration Control Post at Complex Sultan Abu\nBakar, Tanjung Kupang, Johore;\n\n(C) D01 Padang Besar, Perlis;\n\n(D) D06 Bukit Kayu Hitam, Kedah;\n\n(E) D20 Sungai Tujoh, Miri, Sarawak; or\n\n(F) D22A Immigration Control Post Tedungan, Limbang,\nSarawak;\n\n(e) the expatriate is not allowed to apply for any other p asses under the\nImmigration Regulations 1963 [L.N. 228/1963];\n\n(f) the expatriate shall have a travel air ticket to Malaysia and back to India or\nto any country if the expatriate travels by air;\n\n(g) the expatriate shall produce work information , in business, professional\nor technical field , and long term pass  from any country where the\nexpatriate works;\n\n(h) the expatriate shall, on arrival ,  produce a proof that he has sufficient\npocket-money, credit card or bank card, and produce his itinerary in\nMalaysia; and\n\n(i) the expatriate is allowed to re -register to enter Malaysia after the period\nof three months from the date he leaves Malaysia.\n\nMade 29 March 2017\n[KDN(S):IM 03/208/4 Jld 3; PN(PU2)482/II]\n\nDATO' SERI DR. AHMAD ZAHID BIN HAMIDI\nMinister of Home Affairs"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 2"
    }
   }
  ]
 },
