 "MY-H6991": {
  "lawId": "MY-H6991",
  "sourceLang": "ms",
  "targetLang": "en",
  "engine": "official-extract",
  "model": null,
  "promptVersion": null,
  "translatedAt": "2026-10-28",
  "reviewed": "official",
  "note": "公报原生英文版（与马来文版同一公报并置），逐字照录，非机译。",
  "articles": [
   {
    "no": 1,
    "text": {
     "en": "1. (1) This order may be cited as the Passports (Exemption of Visa to Tourist\n\nWho is Citizen of India) Order 2017.\n\n(2) This Order has effect for the period from 1 April 2017 to 31 March 2018.\n\nExemption"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 1"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 2,
    "text": {
     "en": "2. The Minister exempts a tourist who is a citizen of India from the requirement of\n\nvisa under subsection 2(1) of the Act subject to the following conditions:\n\n(a) the tourist shall be registered in the electronic travel registration and\n\ninformation system and the registration may be made—\n\n(i) by the tourist himself; or\n\n(ii) on behalf of the tourist, by a travel agency in India which is\n\nregistered with the Malaysian Mission Office in India;\n\n(b) the tourist shall travel to Malaysia within three months after he is\n\nregistered in the electronic travel registration and information system;\n\n(c) the period of visit of the tourist is limited to fifteen days only and shall not\n\nbe extended;\n\n(d) the tourist shall enter and exit from Malaysia only through authorized\n\npoints of entry as follows:\n\n(i) by air—\n\n(A) U21A Kuala Lumpur International Airport, Sepang;\n\n(B) U05 Pulau Pinang Airport, Bayan Lepas, Penang;\n\n(C) U15 Sultan Ismail Airport, Johor Bahru, Johore;\n\n(D) U17 Kuching Airport, First Division, Sarawak;\n\n(E) U29 Kota Kinabalu Airport, Sabah;\n\n(F) U02 Langkawi International Airport, Kedah;\n\n(G) U14 Melaka Airport, Batu Berendam, Malacca;\n\n(H) U16 Labuan Airport, Federal Territory; or\n\n(I) U23 Miri Airport, Fourth Division, Sarawak; or\n\n(ii) by land—\n\n(A) D11 Sultan Iskandar Building, Johore;\n\n(B) D12A Immigration Control Post at Complex Sultan Abu\n\nBakar, Tanjung Kupang, Johore;\n\n(C) D01 Padang Besar, Perlis;\n\n(D) D06 Bukit Kayu Hitam, Kedah;\n\n(E) D20 Sungai Tujoh, Miri, Sarawak; or\n\n(F) D22A Immigration Control Post Tedungan, Limbang,\n\nSarawak;\n\n(e) the tourist is not allowed to apply for any other passes under the\n\nImmigration Regulations 1963 [L.N. 228/1963];\n\n(f) the tourist shall take a direct flight from India to Malaysia or enter\n\nMalaysia through Singapore, Thailand or Brunei, and have a return air\n\nticket direct to India, or through Singapore, Thailand or Brunei if the\n\ntourist travels by air;\n\n(g) the tourist shall, on arrival, produce proof of sufficient pocket-money,\n\ncredit card or bank card, and produce his itinerary in Malaysia; and\n\n(h) the tourist is allowed to re-register to enter Malaysia after the period of\n\nthree months from the date of he leaves Malaysia.\n\nMade 29 March 2017\n\n[KDN(S):IM 03/208/4 Jld 3; PN(PU2)482/II]\n\nDATO' SERI DR. AHMAD ZAHID BIN HAMIDI\n\nMinister of Home Affairs"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 2"
    }
   }
  ]
 },
