 "MY-H7011": {
  "lawId": "MY-H7011",
  "sourceLang": "ms",
  "targetLang": "en",
  "engine": "official-extract",
  "model": null,
  "promptVersion": null,
  "translatedAt": "2026-10-28",
  "reviewed": "official",
  "note": "公报原生英文版（与马来文版同一公报并置），逐字照录，非机译。",
  "articles": [
   {
    "no": 1,
    "text": {
     "en": "1. (1) This order may be cited as t he Income Tax (Exemption)\nOrder 2022.\n\n (2) This Order has effect for the year of assessment 2022.\n\nApplication"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 1"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 2,
    "text": {
     "en": "2. This Order shall apply to a company which has income received in Malaysia from\noutside Malaysia from 1 July 2022.\n\nInterpretation"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 2"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 3,
    "text": {
     "en": "3. In this Order—\n\n\"income received in Malaysia  from outside Malaysia\" means income arising from\noutside Malaysia which is brought into Malaysia;\n\n\"company\" means a company  which is  incorporated or registered  under the\nCompanies Act 2016 [Act 777] and resident in Malaysia.\n\nExemption"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 3"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 4,
    "text": {
     "en": "4. (1) The Minister exempts the application of the provision of subparagraph 2(2)\nof Part I of Schedule 1 to the Act , to a company in respect of its chargeable income\nin relation to any income received in Malaysia from outside Malaysia  in the basis period\nfor the year of assessment 2022.\n\n (2) For the purpose s of subparagraph (1) , the chargeable income\nin relation to any income received in Malaysia from outside Malaysia in the basis period\nfor the year of assessment 2022 shall be determined in accordance with\nthe following formula:\n\n(3) Where chargeable income in relation to the income received\nin Malaysia from outside Malaysia  has been determined under subparagraph (2),\nany excess of the chargeable income of that company which is subject to tax shall be\ncharged to income tax for the year of assessment 2022 under subparagraph 2(1)\nor 2(2) of Part I of Schedule 1 to the Act, as the case may  be.\n\n(4)  Nothing in subparagraph (1) shall absolve or be deemed to have absolved\na company from complying with any requirement to submit any return\nor statement of accounts or to furnish any other information under the provisions\nof the Act.\n\nA\n—\nB\nx C\nwhere A is the statutory incom e in relation to the\nincome received in Malaysia from out side Malaysia\nin the basis period for the year of assessment 2022;\n\n B is the aggregate income in the basis period for the\nyear of assessment 2022;\n\n C is the chargeable income of the company in the\nbasis period for the year of assessment 2022.\n\nMade 1 April 2022\n[Perb. MOF.TAX(S)700-1/1/33; LHDN.AY.A.600-12/1(29)-191; PN(PU2)80/JLD. 105]\n\n                     TENGKU DATUK SERI UTAMA ZAFRUL BIN TENGKU ABDUL AZIZ\n                                             Minister of Finance\n\n[To be laid before the Dewan Rakyat pursuant to subsection 1 27(4) of the\nIncome Tax Act 1967]"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 4"
    }
   }
  ]
 },
