 "MY-H7045": {
  "lawId": "MY-H7045",
  "sourceLang": "ms",
  "targetLang": "en",
  "engine": "official-extract",
  "model": null,
  "promptVersion": null,
  "translatedAt": "2026-10-28",
  "reviewed": "official",
  "note": "公报原生英文版（与马来文版同一公报并置），逐字照录，非机译。",
  "articles": [
   {
    "no": 1,
    "text": {
     "en": "1. (1) This order may be cited as the Malaysia Deposit Insurance Corporation\n(Basis for Calculation of First Levy and Annual Levy in respect of Insurer Members)\n(Amendment) Order 2026.\n\n(2) This Order shall have effect from the assessment year of 2026.\n\nGeneral amendment"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 1"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 2,
    "text": {
     "en": "2. The Malaysia Deposit Insurance Corporation (Basis for Calculation of First Levy\nand Annual Levy in respect of Insurer Members) Order 2023 [P.U. (A) 223/2023],\nwhich is referred to as the \"principal Order\" in this Order, is amended—\n\n(a) by substituting for the words \"total net contributions\" wherever appearing\nthe words \"total net takaful revenue\"; and\n\n(b) by substituting for the words \" total net premiums \" wherever appearing\nthe words \"total net insurance revenue\".\n\nNew paragraph 5"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 2"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 3,
    "text": {
     "en": "3. The principal Order is amended by inserting after paragraph 4\nthe following paragraph:\n\n\"Transitional arrangement in respect of family takaful and life insurance"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 3"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 5,
    "text": {
     "en": "5. For the purposes of subsubparagraph 2(4) (a), subparagraph 3(1),\nsubsubparagraph 3(3) (a) and subsubsubparagraph 3(3) (b)(i), the valuation of\nfamily takaful liabilities or life insurance liabilities in respect of medical and health\ninsurance or  medical and health  takaful for the assessment years of 2026\nand 2027—\n\n(a) in respect of the valuation of liabilities of an insurer member which\nbecomes a member institution on or before 31 December 2024,\nthe valuation of family takaful liabilities or life insurance liabilities\nin respect of medical and health insurance or medical and health\ntakaful shall be as at 31 December 2024 instead of 31 December of\nthe preceding assessment year; or\n\n(b) in respect of the valuation of liabilities of an insurer member which\nbecomes a member institution  after 31 December 2024,\nthe valuation of family takaful liabilities or life insurance liabilities\nin respect of medical and health insurance or medical and health\ntakaful shall be as at 31 December of the assessment year\nin which the insurer member becomes a member institution\ninstead of 31 December of the preceding assessment year.\".\n\nMade 20 February 2026\n[MOF.SBM(R) 600-41/39/102 (13); PIDM/PN/3/2026; PN(PU2)689/JLD.9]\n\nDATUK SERI AMIR HAMZAH BIN AZIZAN\nFinance Minister II"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 5"
    }
   }
  ]
 },
 "MY-H7046": {
  "lawId": "MY-H7046",
  "sourceLang": "ms",
  "targetLang": "en",
  "engine": "official-extract",
  "model": null,
  "promptVersion": null,
  "translatedAt": "2026-10-28",
  "reviewed": "official",
  "note": "公报原生英文版（与马来文版同一公报并置），逐字照录，非机译。",
  "articles": [
   {
    "no": 1,
    "text": {
     "en": "1. (1)     This order may be cited as the Labuan Business Activity Tax\n(Exemption) Order 2013.\n\n(2)  This Order shall have effect from the year of assessment 2013 and\nsubsequent years of assessment.\n\nInterpretation"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 1"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 2,
    "text": {
     "en": "2.  In this Order—\n\n\"Global Incentives for Trading\" means a programme of incentives for the Labuan\nInternational Commodity T rading Company to use Malaysia as their international\ntrading base to undertake qualifying activity;\n\n\"Labuan International Commodity Trading Compan y\" means a Labuan company\nwhich—\n\n(a) is incorporated or registered under the Labuan Companies Act 1990\n[Act 441];\n\n(b) is licensed under section 92 of the Labuan Financial Services and\nSecurities Act 2010 [Act 704];\n\n(c) maintains a registered office in Labuan but is allowed to establish its\noperational office anywhere in Malaysia; and\n\n(d) undertakes a  qualifying activity under the Global Incentives for Trading\nprogramme;\n\n\"qualifying activity \" means the trading of  physical and related derivative\ninstruments of liquefied natural  gas in any currency other than Ringgit.\n\nExemption"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 2"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 3,
    "text": {
     "en": "3. (1) The Minister exempts the Labuan International Commodity Trading\nCompany from the payment of tax in respect of its income derived from qualifying\nactivity.\n\n (2) The exemption referred to in subparagraph (1) shall be for a period of\nthree consecutive years commencing from the first year of its operation.\n\nSeparate source and account"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 3"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 4,
    "text": {
     "en": "4. (1) Where a Labuan International Commodity Trading Company carries on a\nqualifying activity referred to in paragraph 2, and any other activity or business, each of\nsuch activity or business shall be treated as a separate and distinct source of activity or\nbusiness.\n\n(2) The Labuan International Commodity Trading Company which is\nexempted under paragraph 3, shall maintain a separate account for the income derived\nfrom each activity referred to in subparagraph (1).\n\nMade 13 March 2013\n[Perb.(C)0.217(SJ.21)JLD.8(SK.5); LHDN 01/35/(S)/42/51/231-12; PN(PU2)491]\n\nDATO' SERI AHMAD HUSNI MOHAMAD HANADZLAH\n                           Second Minister of Finance\n\n[To be laid before the Dewan Rakyat pursuant to subsection 26(2) of the Labuan Business\nActivity Tax Act 1990]"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 4"
    }
   }
  ]
 },
