 "MY-H712": {
  "lawId": "MY-H712",
  "sourceLang": "ms",
  "targetLang": "en",
  "engine": "official-extract",
  "model": null,
  "promptVersion": null,
  "translatedAt": "2026-10-28",
  "reviewed": "official",
  "note": "公报原生英文版（与马来文版同一公报并置），逐字照录，非机译。",
  "articles": [
   {
    "no": 1,
    "text": {
     "en": "1. (1) This order may be cited as the Water Services Industry (Licensing)\n\n(Exemption) Order 2025.\n\n(2) This Order has effect for the period from 1 April 2025 to 31 March 2026.\n\nInterpretation"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 1"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 2,
    "text": {
     "en": "2. In this Order—\n\n\"Kawasan Terengganu Tengah\" has the meaning assigned to it in the Lembaga\n\nKemajuan Terengganu Tengah Act 1973 [Act 104];\n\n\"Lembaga Kemajuan Terengganu Tengah\" means the Lembaga Kemajuan\n\nTerengganu Tengah established under section 3 of the Lembaga Kemajuan Terengganu\n\nTengah Act 1973.\n\nExemption"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 2"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 3,
    "text": {
     "en": "3. The Minister exempts the Lembaga Kemajuan Terengganu Tengah from\n\nthe requirement for individual licence under section 4 of the Act for the operation\n\nand maintenance of the public sewerage system in the Kawasan Terengganu Tengah,\n\nTerengganu.\n\nConditions of exemption"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 3"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 4,
    "text": {
     "en": "4. The exemption under paragraph 3 is subject to the conditions that the Lembaga\n\nKemajuan Terengganu Tengah shall—\n\n(a) obtain financial allocations to carry out a sewerage catchment master plan\n\nstudy for the purpose of identifying the needs for refurbishment and\n\nupgrading of the sewerage system in the Kawasan Terengganu Tengah;\n\n(b) obtain financial allocations to carry out refurbishment and upgrading\n\nworks for the sewerage system based on the outcome of the approved\n\nsewerage catchment master plan study;\n\n(c) carry out desludging and desilting works in oxidation ponds periodically;\n\nand\n\n(d) appoint an accredited person to carry out an effluent quality sampling in\n\nthe sewage treatment plant periodically, at least once a month, after the\n\ndesludging and desilting works in the oxidation ponds have been carried\n\nout.\n\nMade 26 March 2025\n\n[PETRA.BAP.100-1/1/3(S)KLT.4; PN(PU2)660/JLD.19]\n\nDATO' SRI HAJI FADILLAH BIN HAJI YUSOF\n\nMinister of Energy Transition and Water Transformation"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 4"
    }
   }
  ]
 },
 "MY-H713": {
  "lawId": "MY-H713",
  "sourceLang": "ms",
  "targetLang": "en",
  "engine": "official-extract",
  "model": null,
  "promptVersion": null,
  "translatedAt": "2026-10-28",
  "reviewed": "official",
  "note": "公报原生英文版（与马来文版同一公报并置），逐字照录，非机译。",
  "articles": [
   {
    "no": 1,
    "text": {
     "en": "1. (1)  This order may be cited as the  Credit Reporting Agencies\n(Minimum Amount of Paid-Up Capital) Order 2026.\n\n (2)  This Order comes into operation on 1 March 2026.\n\nMinimum amount of paid-up capital"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 1"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 2,
    "text": {
     "en": "2. The minimum amount of paid -up capital of a credit reporting agency shall be\nfive million ringgit.\n\nTransitional"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 2"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 3,
    "text": {
     "en": "3. Any credit reporting agency whose paid -up capital is less than the minimum\namount as specified in paragraph 2 before the date of the coming into operation\nof this Order shall, not later than 1 January 2029, maintain and increase its paid-up capital\nto comply with the minimum amount.\n\nMade 26 February 2026\n[MOF.PPK(S)600-1/1/2 JLD.3; PN(PU2)706/IV]\n\nDATUK SERI AMIR HAMZAH BIN AZIZAN\nFinance Minister II"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 3"
    }
   }
  ]
 },
 "MY-H717": {
  "lawId": "MY-H717",
  "sourceLang": "ms",
  "targetLang": "en",
  "engine": "official-extract",
  "model": null,
  "promptVersion": null,
  "translatedAt": "2026-10-28",
  "reviewed": "official",
  "note": "公报原生英文版（与马来文版同一公报并置），逐字照录，非机译。",
  "articles": [
   {
    "no": 1,
    "text": {
     "en": "1. This order may be cited as the Medical Device (Exemption) Order 2016.\n\nInterpretation"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 1"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 2,
    "text": {
     "en": "2. In this Order—\n\n\"clinical research\" means a systematic investigation or study to human beings\n\nundertaken to assess the safety and performance of a medical device;\n\n\"personal use\" means a medical device which is brought into Malaysia for the use\n\nof a particular individual only and not to be placed in the market;\n\n\"special access medical device\" means a medical device for the use of medical\n\npractitioners in emergency situations or in the event that conventional medical\n\ntreatment has failed, is unavailable or unsuitable;\n\n\"custom-made medical device\" means a medical device made with specific design\n\ncharacteristics in accordance with a medical practitioner's written prescription and is\n\nintended to be used for a particular patient.\n\nExemption from registration of medical devices"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 2"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 3,
    "text": {
     "en": "3. (1) The Minister exempts any medical device from section 5 of the Act if the\n\nmedical device is—\n\n(a) for the purpose of personal use;\n\n(b) for the purpose of demonstration for marketing;\n\n(c) for the purpose of education;\n\n(d) for the purpose of clinical research or performance evaluation of\n\nmedical device;\n\n(e) a custom-made medical device; or\n\n(f) a special access medical device.\n\n(2) A person who imports or manufactures any medical device under\n\nsubparagraph (1)(b), (c), (d), (e) or (f) shall notify the Authority in writing of the\n\nexemption.\n\nExemption from establishment license"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 3"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 4,
    "text": {
     "en": "4. A person who imports or manufactures medical device under paragraph 3 is\n\nexempted from the requirement of an establishment license under subsection 15(1) of\n\nthe Act.\n\nExemption from conformity assessment for Class A medical device"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 4"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 5,
    "text": {
     "en": "5. A Class A medical device is exempted from the conformity assessment\n\nprocedures by a conformity assessment body under section 7 of the Act.\n\nMade 8 April 2016\n\n[KKMMDA(S)100/1-1-1; PN(PU2)711/III]\n\nDATUK SERI DR. S. SUBRAMANIAM\n\nMinister of Health"
    },
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 5"
    }
   }
  ]
 },
